 Dementia
 Heart disease
 Homocystinuria (when your body can’t process methionine)
 Hypothyroidism (underactive thyroid)
 Osteoporosis
 Psoriasis

#### What are the signs I may need a homocysteine test?

You may need a homocysteine blood test if you have symptoms of a vitamin B deficiency. Common symptoms of vitamin B deficiencies include: [...] Homocysteine (Hcy) is an amino acid. It’s a chemical in your blood that helps create proteins. Vitamin B12, vitamin B6 and vitamin B9 (folate) break down homocysteine to generate other chemicals your body needs.

