Content: Diminished ovarian reserve is when you have fewer eggs left in your ovaries compared to others your age. Diminished ovarian reserve is when you have fewer eggs in your ovaries compared to people your age. Your odds of conceiving may be smaller when your ovarian reserve is low, but you only need one egg to get pregnant. Other times, genetics or medical treatments cause diminished ovarian reserve. Ovarian reserve testing is a way for providers to estimate how many eggs you have left. There is no way to reverse diminished ovarian reserve or produce more eggs. Success rates with IVF vary depending on the cause of low ovarian reserve, how many eggs you have and how your body responds to fertility medication.
