Content: Summary Diacylglycerol kinase κ (DGKK) is a lipid‐modifying enzyme that phosphorylates diacylglycerol into phosphatidic acid, thereby regulating key signaling pathways that influence both neural function and urogenital development. In the context of male genital formation, multiple independent studies have identified that genetic variants in DGKK are strongly associated with an increased risk of hypospadias, particularly in cases exhibiting mild to moderate phenotypes. Expression analyses in [...] Citations:1-14

