Content: The induction of the E cell to form endoderm also depends on the MES-1 and Wnt pathways. Endoderm fate specification requires the Wnt ligand (MOM-2 in _C. elegans_, expressed in the P 2 cell), the transmembrane Frizzled receptor (MOM-5), and other conserved Wnt pathway components (Rocheleau _et al_. 1997; Thorpe _et al_. 1997; Schlesinger _et al_. 1999). Activation of this pathway ultimately results in nuclear export of the transcription factor POP-1 in the E cell, which allows [...] Asymmetric cell division is essential for the creation of cell types with different identities and functions. The endomesodermal precursor cell (EMS) of the 4-cell _Caenorhabditis elegans_ embryo undergoes an asymmetric division in response to partially redundant signaling pathways. One pathway involves a Wnt signal from the neighboring P 2 cell, while the other pathway is defined by the receptor-like MES-1 transmembrane protein localized at the EMS-P 2 cell contact and the cytoplasmic kinase [...] Helen Lamb, McKenzi Fernholz, Małgorzata J Liro, Krista M Myles, Holly Anderson, Lesilee S Rose, The Rac1 homolog CED-10 is a component of the MES-1/SRC-1 pathway for asymmetric division of the _Caenorhabditis elegans_ EMS blastomere, _Genetics_, Volume 229, Issue 4, April 2025, iyaf020,  Select Format Download citation Close  
