### Spatiotemporal regulation of intracellular trafficking of Toll-like receptor 9 by an inhibitory receptor, Ly49Q [...] Ly49Q is a member of the lectin-type NK receptor family but is preferentially expressed in pDCs, macrophages, and neutrophils (Omatsu et al., 2005; Toyama-Sorimachi et al., 2005). Ly49Q has an ITIM in its cytoplasmic region (Makrigiannis et al., 2002; Toyama-Sorimachi et al., 2004) and recruits SHP-1 and SHP-2 in a manner dependent on tyrosine phosphorylation (Toyama-Sorimachi et al., 2004). As with other NK receptors, Ly49Q associates with classical MHC class I (MHC-I) (Tai et al., 2007). [...] However, Ly49Q and MHC-I interact mainly through a _cis_-configuration (Tai et al., 2007), and the physiological significance of the receptor’s _cis_-interaction is still largely obscure. We previously demonstrated that Ly49Q controls the trafficking of raft membrane domains through a mechanism that includes the ITIM- and stimuli-dependent recruitment of signaling molecules such as SHPs and Src-family kinases (Sasawatari et al., 2010). This machinery contributes to neutrophil chemotactic [...] Ly49Q is an ITIM-bearing MHC class I receptor that is highly expressed in plasmacytoid dendritic cells (pDCs). Ly49Q is required for the TLR9-mediated IFN-I production in pDCs, although the mechanism is not fully understood. We here demonstrate that Ly49Q protects pDCs from pyroptotic cell death induced by CpG oligodeoxynucleotides (CpG). In the Ly49Q-deficient (_Klra17−/−_) mouse spleen, the number of ssDNA-positive pDCs increased significantly after CpG treatment, strongly suggesting that [...] migration by accelerating the formation of cellular polarity. In pDCs, Ly49Q is pivotal for IFN-I production, given that IFN-I production from pDCs is diminished in Ly49Q-deficient (_Klra17−/−_) mice upon TLR9 stimulation (Tai et al., 2008). Consistent with this finding, _Klra17−/−_ mice are more susceptible to CMV infection than _Klra17+/+_ mice (Tai et al., 2008). Therefore, even though Ly49Q includes an ITIM, it positively regulates IFN-I production in pDCs (Tai et al., 2008). We also
Score: 0.62330866


