hages develop in a Myb-dependent manner . Yolk sac erythro-myeloid progenitors can generate macrophages without a monocyte intermediate, but they also colonize the fetal liver where they give rise to Myb-expressing fetal monocytes . In turn, these fetal monocytes can differentiate into tissue-resident macrophages . There is, however, a paucity of information on the development of tissue-resident macrophages in
