Research [...] Amitriptyline is one of several prophylactic treatments for chronic daily headache, and can be used in conjunction with nonpharmacologic therapies such as relaxation techniques and cognitive behavior therapy 6.
   The medication should be used with caution, as it can have side effects such as daytime fatigue, and patients should be monitored for medication overuse 4, 6. [...] A retrospective cohort study found that approximately 3/4 of patients experienced improvement in headache symptoms, and 85% were still taking amitriptyline at the last follow-up appointment 4.
   The study also found that low doses of amitriptyline (≤10 mg daily) were effective and well-tolerated, and may improve medication persistence 4.
