ng M2 [...] In humans, thermogenic fat was believed to exist restrictively to infancy to generate heat and fight against hypothermia under cold environments. However, in 2009 a series of milestone publications identified the presence of functional thermogenic fat in the upper supraclavicular region of adult humans (21–23). Thermogenic activity, determined by 18F-fluorodeoxyglucose uptake, was induced in the supraclavicular area following short cold exposure, and its biopsy specimens showed the molecular
