Content: Brown adipose tissue (BAT) is the primary organ for non-shivering thermogenesis in mammals and can dissipate chemical energy as heat upon cold stimulus.1 BAT has a high density of mitochondria that contain uncoupling protein-1 (UCP1) in the inner mitochondrial membrane. To generate heat, UCP1 releases the stored mitochondrial proton gradient generated by the electron transport chain and fueled by fatty acids.2,3 Activation of BAT by cold exposure, local hyperthermia, or β-adrenergic agonists [...] response to decreasing ambient temperature (from 30°C to 22°C and from 22°C to STEMCT) (Figure 6A) or cold exposure to 4°C for 2 h (Figure S6C). Intriguingly, _CEBPB_ expression was also cold induced, along with _UCP1_, in supraclavicular BAT samples obtained from overweight or obese women following ∼6 h of mild cold exposure (∼20°C) compared with ∼6 h exposure to TN (∼28°C) (Figures 6B and 6C). Moreover, _CEBPB_ mRNA was induced by norepinephrine in primary adipocytes from supraclavicular BAT [...] ∗∗_p_<0.01, ∗∗∗_p_<0.001, as analyzed by two-way ANOVA with Tukey’s test (F). ∗∗_p_<0.01 (22°C: _Hdac3_ _f/f_, _Pgc-1α_ _f/f_ versus _Ucp1-cre_; _Hdac3_ _f/f_, _Pgc-1α_ _f/f_), #_p_<0.05, ###_p_<0.001 (1-day recovery: _Hdac3_ _f/f_, _Pgc-1α_ _f/f_ versus _Ucp1-cre_; _Hdac3_ _f/f_, _Pgc-1α_ _f/f_) by Welch's t test (G). NS, not significant. Data are represented as mean± SEM. [...] may provide beneficial effects to human metabolism through the combustion of stored calories to counteract type 2 diabetes, insulin resistance, obesity, and cardiometabolic disease.4,5,6,7,8,9,10 However, there exists great individual variation of both BAT mass and activity levels, which are influenced by the length of daylight, environmental temperature, age, sex, body mass index (BMI), plasma glucose levels, and diabetic status, likely driven in part by genetic and epigenetic [...] external temperature of 15°C (Figure S5B), corresponding to the temperature that has been considered to be painfully cold in mammals.39 A shorter time course study demonstrated a strong induction of PGC-1α by just 2 h of exposure to 15°C (Figure S5C). These data suggest that STEMCT circumvents the genetic requirement of HDAC3 coactivator function required for basal thermogenic gene expression through cold-induced expression of _Pgc-1_ α.
