torage, or disposal. [...] should be implemented to reduce exposure risk and contaminant spread (e.g., limit movement and activities within the suspected area, implement proper personnel decontamination procedures). • Soil: B. anthracis spores are resistant to adverse environmental conditions and may remain viable in soil for decades. Re-aerosolization may occur when contaminated soil is disturbed. • Surfaces: B. anthracis spores are resistant to adverse environmental conditions and may remain viable on surfaces for
