Migraine and SSRIs

# Migraine and SSRIs

Living with migraine and conditions like anxiety or depression can feel overwhelming — especially when you’re taking medications for both. If you’ve been prescribed antidepressants, you may wonder how these two conditions — and their treatments — interact. Can SSRIs trigger migraine or make it worse? Or, could they actually help alleviate migraine symptoms? [...] SSRIs block this reuptake process. So, instead of getting reabsorbed too quickly, serotonin stays in the space between your brain cells — known as the synapse — for longer. More serotonin translates to better moods and regulated emotions. However, the process is not as fast as it may sound. It usually takes a few weeks for SSRIs to build up enough to result in any noticeable mood changes.
