Content: ### Fluoxetine (Prozac, Prozac Weekly, Sarafem)

## Fluoxetine (Prozac, Prozac Weekly, Sarafem)

Fluoxetine is a second-line agent for patients with chronic migraines. It is an atypical, nontricyclic antidepressant with potent, specific inhibition of 5-HT uptake and with fewer anticholinergic and cardiovascular side effects than tricyclic antidepressants have.

### Sertraline (Zoloft)

## Sertraline (Zoloft) [...] Amitriptyline has efficacy for migraine prophylaxis that is independent of its antidepressant effect. Its mechanism of action is unknown, but it inhibits the activity of such diverse agents as histamine, 5-HT, and acetylcholine.

### Nortriptyline (Pamelor)

## Nortriptyline (Pamelor) [...] SSRIs have limited efficacy for migraine prophylaxis in adults. Due to a lack of clinical studies, they are not recommended for this purpose in children.

### Paroxetine (Paxil, Paxil CR, Pexeva, Brisdelle)

## Paroxetine (Paxil, Paxil CR, Pexeva, Brisdelle)

Paroxetine is an atypical, nontricyclic antidepressant with potent, specific inhibition of 5-HT uptake inhibition and fewer anticholinergic and cardiovascular adverse effects than tricyclic antidepressants have. [...] Doxepin has efficacy for migraine prophylaxis that is independent of its antidepressant effect. Its mechanism of action is unknown, but it increases the concentration of serotonin and norepinephrine in the CNS by inhibiting their reuptake by presynaptic neuronal membrane. It also inhibits histamine and acetylcholine activity.

### Protriptyline (Vivactil)

## Protriptyline (Vivactil) [...] Nortriptyline has efficacy for migraine prophylaxis that is independent of its antidepressant effect. Its mechanism of action is unknown, but it inhibits the activity of such diverse agents as histamine, 5-HT, and acetylcholine.

