Title: Validation and clinical implementation of cerebrospinal ...
URL: https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lanepe/article/PIIS2666-7762(25)00101-2/fulltext
Content: Implications of all the available evidence

Our study confirmed that CSF CRP is an excellent diagnostic marker for bacterial meningitis, and that its implementation in clinical practice is simple and available at low cost. This makes it a valuable tool for diagnosing bacterial meningitis by enabling timely and accurate treatment, which is essential for a good prognosis.

Introduction

Accurate and timely diagnosis of bacterial meningitis is crucial for improving outcome.100101-2/fulltext#)

