e management of the disease. Even short delays in the diagnosis and treatment increase the rate of sequelae and mortality.11 The CSF culture is the gold standard for the diagnosis of bacterial meningitis. The diminished sensitivity of the CSF culture in the patients who received antibiotics before the LP and the 72-h test period
