n in these [...] cancer in obese patients. In sum, our findings reinforce the beneficial role of bariatric surgery in curtailing the risk of colorectal cancer for morbidly obese individuals, particularly emphasizing its pronounced impact on females. This finding may help clinicians develop more personalized treatment strategies to reduce the risk of colorectal cancer in obese patients. Nonetheless, subsequent studies should delve deeper into the enduring effects of varied bariatric surgical methods and
