Title: The effect of bariatric surgery on reducing the risk of colorectal cancer
URL: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36446716/
Content: Display options 

 Format 

Abstract

Background: The published literature presents conflicting results regarding the impact of bariatric surgery on the incidence of colorectal cancer. There are important new studies that have addressed this question with longer follow-up.

Objective: To investigate the effect of bariatric surgery on the risk of developing colorectal cancer in patients with obesity.

Setting: Meta-analysis. [...] Conclusion: Patients who underwent bariatric surgery had a 37% reduction in the risk of developing colorectal cancer compared with patients with obesity who had no surgery.

Keywords: Bariatric surgery; Bowel cancer; Colon cancer; Colorectal cancer; Gastric bypass; Meta-analysis; Rectal cancer; Sleeve gastrectomy.

