Content: Bariatric surgery could also potentially negatively affect mental health.2 Long-term observational data show a higher risk of suicide among adults undergoing bariatric surgery than among non-surgically treated, BMI-matched comparators.12, 13 When stratified by age, the increased risk of suicide was primarily seen in younger adults (18–34 years).12 Studies in adults also show an increased risk of substance use disorder, particularly with alcohol, after bariatric surgery.14, 15 [...] Implications of all the available evidence

