d healthcare professionals to consider is the potential for psychiatric complications arising from bariatric surgery. These may include depression, anxiety disorders, eating disorders, dissatisfaction due to unmet weight loss expectations, body image disturbances, psychotic syndromes, and, most importantly, suicide risk.( sequelae may vary depending on the type of procedure undergone. For instance, a cohort study conducted in Taiwan tracking
