Title: How Bariatric Surgery Can Affect Your Mental Health
URL: https://www.texascenterforsurgery.com/blog/2024/07/25/how-bariatric-surgery-can-affect-216365/
Content: For many patients, bariatric surgery has multiple benefits to their psychological and emotional well-being. While emotions will always ebb and flow when it comes to major life changes or unforeseen events, the potential mental health improvements from surgery are worth noting.

### Improvement in Body Image and Self-Esteem [...] Bariatric surgery can contribute to mental health improvements for many patients. We at the Texas Center for Bariatrics & Advanced Surgery would like to explore different aspects of mental health before and after surgery so you understand what to expect.

Assessing Mental Health Before Undergoing Bariatric Surgery [...] With decreased appetite and stomach capacity, bariatric surgery patients may find changes in the way they eat and engage with food. If you ate as a coping mechanism, discussing these matters with a mental health professional can help you understand past behaviors and develop new ones.

### Better Physical Health Contributes to Better Mental Health [...] Achieving a healthier body mass can work wonders for your cardiovascular health, respiratory health, and joint health. Patients may have reduced severity of sleep apnea and other comorbidities. This enhanced quality of life can go a long way toward improving someone’s overall outlook.

Make the Choice That’s Right for Your Needs [...] The entire team at our bariatric surgery center in Plano, TX, is committed to your weight loss and health journey. That doesn’t just mean overcoming obesity and its effects on general wellness. This also means helping patients feel good about their decision and the many benefits bariatric surgery can have in their lives.
Score: 0.8660535


Title: Unlocking Mental Health Benefits with Weight Loss Surgery
URL: https://www.queens.org/mental-health-benefits-weight-loss-surgery/
Content: The Cycle of Positive Change

The journey doesn’t stop with surgery. The positive mental health effects of weight loss surgery often inspire a cycle of continued improvement. Engaging in physical activities becomes more accessible and enjoyable, further enhancing mental health. Moreover, the support systems in place for post-surgery patients, including counseling and support groups, provide a foundation for sustaining these mental health gains. [...] Weight loss surgery can also play a pivotal role in reducing the symptoms of depression and anxiety, conditions often intertwined with obesity. The psychosocial stress and physical limitations associated with being overweight can exacerbate these mental health challenges. As you begin to see and feel the physical improvements post-surgery, you may also notice a lightening of the mental health burdens that have weighed you down. Engaging in activities that were once off-limits due to physical or [...] Post-surgery, one of the first psychological improvements many notice is a boost in self-esteem and a more positive body image. This shift towards self-acceptance and confidence can ripple out into all areas of your life, improving social interactions, professional performance, and overall engagement with life’s activities. This newfound confidence is more than skin deep; it’s a profound inner change that encourages a more fulfilling and vibrant lifestyle.

Alleviating Depression and Anxiety [...] Beginning aweight loss surgeryis not just about transforming your physical appearance; it’s about reshaping your mental landscape as well. Obesity often carries with it not just physical but psychological burdens, including depression, anxiety, and a diminished quality of life. However, the aftermath of weight loss surgery can open the door to significant mental health improvements, marking a new chapter in both your physical and emotional well-being.

Enhanced Self-Esteem and Body Image [...] In embracing the changes brought on by weight loss surgery, you’re not just transforming your body; you’re opening a pathway to a more engaged, active, and mentally healthy life.

