he potential to significantly influence outcomes post-bariatric surgery. Research indicates that patients with depression who undergo bariatric procedures tend to experience less weight loss compared to those without depression.( Similarly, a history of binge-eating disorder can also affect weight loss outcomes post-surgery.( Moreover, individuals with alcohol use disorder exhibit higher rates of alcohol consumption beyond the initial 2-year
