ositively with HDL, albumin, and the A/G ratio (Fig. 6I–P). Therefore, transplanting basophils with Atg5 deficiency could improve the lupus condition by modulating lipid and amino acid metabolism through alterations in gut microbiota populations, particularly those of Ligilactobacillus and Faecalitalea. These bacteria may ameliorate lupus by promoting beneficial metabolites (GLA, DLPC, and OPPC) and reducing harmful metabolites (arginine, methylmalonic acid, and 2-hydroxyglutaric acid), thus
