s involved in breast carcinogenesis are also connected to the regulation of fetal growth, the association between birth weight and breast cancer could be confounded by genetic factors. There could also be confounding from other factors associated with breast cancer and birth weight, including socioeconomic status, lifestyle, and dietary habits. Previous attempts to control for confounding by adjusting for
