Title: Preterm birth, birth weight, and subsequent risk of female breast ...
URL: https://www.nature.com/articles/6601357
Content: risk, and this association was independent of age at diagnosis. Some studies have reported the association between birth weight and breast cancer to be J-shaped, with an increased risk also among women with a very low birth weight (Potischman and Troisi, 1999 In-utero and early life exposures in relation to risk of breast cancer. Cancer Causes Control 10: 561–573""); Innes et al, 2000 Birth characteristics and subsequent risk for breast cancer in very young women. Am J Epidemiol 152: [...] The overall risk of cancer among the women was not increased (Table 2). The risk of breast cancer was neither associated with preterm birth nor with low birth weight, but a birth weight of more than 3000 g was associated with an increased risk of breast cancer (Table 2). This increase in breast cancer risk was not dependent on age at onset. [...] In conclusion, we found that neither preterm birth, nor low birth weight, are associated with an increased risk for breast cancer.

