References

   Ekbom A, Erlandsson G, Hsieh C, Trichopoulos D, Adami HO, Cnattingius S (2000) Risk of breast cancer in prematurely born women. _J Natl Cancer Inst_92: 840–841 [...] We have previously reported an increased risk for breast cancer among women born before 32 weeks of gestation( Ekbom et al, 1997 Intrauterine environment and breast cancer risk in women: a population-based study. J Natl Cancer Inst 89: 71–76""); Ekbom et al, 2000 Risk of breast cancer in prematurely born women. J Natl Cancer Inst 92: 840–841"")). Other studies of the association between gestational duration and breast cancer have been mostly negative (Le Marchand et al, 1988 Birth characteristics [...] 1121–1128"")). According to the present data, low birth weight is not a major risk factor for breast cancer.
