Title: Coatomer
URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coatomer
Content: Protein complex that coats membrane-bound transport vesicles The **coatomer** is a protein complex that coats membrane-bound transport vesicles#Transport_vesicles ""Vesicle (biology)""). Coatomers are functionally analogous and evolutionarily homologous to clathrin adaptor proteins, also known as adaptins, which regulate endocytosis from the plasma membrane and transport from the trans-Golgi network to lysosomes. COPI is a coatomer that coats the vesicles ""Vesicle (biology and chemistry)"") transporting proteins from the Golgi complex to the ER. Before the COP I protein can coat vesicles on the Golgi membrane, it must interact with a small GTPase called ARF1 (ADP ribosylation factor). Next, the ARF1 protein recruits COP1 to the golgi complex membrane by interacting with β-COP and γ-COP. COPII is a coatomer that coats the vesicles transporting proteins from the ER to the golgi complex.
