Title: UCP1-independent signaling involving SERCA2b ...
URL: https://www.nature.com/articles/nm.4429
Content: Uncoupling protein 1 (UCP1) plays a central role in nonshivering thermogenesis in brown fat; however, its role in beige fat remains unclear. Here we report a robust UCP1-independent thermogenic mechanism in beige fat that involves enhanced ATP-dependent Ca 2+ cycling by sarco/endoplasmic reticulum Ca 2+-ATPase 2b (SERCA2b) and ryanodine receptor 2 (RyR2). Inhibition of SERCA2b impairs UCP1-independent beige fat thermogenesis in humans and mice as well as in pigs, a species that lacks a [...] Image 13: extended data figure 2
   
