Title: Challenges and resistance mechanisms to EGFR targeted therapies ...
URL: https://www.oncotarget.com/article/28747/text/
Content: Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor (EGFR) targeted therapies have yielded variable results in clinical trials for breast and head and neck cancers, despite EGFR overexpression in these malignancies. This review highlights the role of AXL, MET, and RON families of RTKs in tumor progression and resistance to anti-EGFR therapies, focusing on breast and head and neck cancers. It details how EGFR inhibition affects tumor progression and survival in head and neck cancer, noting that small molecule inhibitors and monoclonal antibodies, such as cetuximab, can lead to trans-activation of other RTKs. The review further explores non-RTK-driven resistance mechanisms in breast cancer, including EGFR activation through EGF-related ligands, nuclear localization of EGFR, and the overexpression of resistance-conferring proteins.
