ased activation motif–containing C-type lectinlike receptor 2 (CLEC-2) is a transmembrane protein that highly expressed in platelets and plays crucial roles in platelet activation (54). Besides contribution to thrombosis, platelet CLEC-2 is also involved in the regulation of tumor metastasis, blood-lymphatic vascular development, and inflammatory bleeding (55). CLEC2 regulates platelet activation mainly by influencing a Src- and spleen tyrosine kinase
