Title: Can eating too much fruit cause type 2 diabetes?
URL: https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/323310
Content: A 2017 study, conducted with data from a Chinese biobank, found a significant association between eating fresh fruit and having a lower risk of diabetes. Participants with diabetes also tended to have a lower risk of developing cardiovascular problems if they ate more fresh fruit.

However, the study’s authors did not determine a specific cause for their findings. It could be that people who regularly eat fresh fruit tend to have a more healthful diet overall. [...] Fruit contains many vitamins, minerals, and fiber, but they also have a high natural sugar content. However, this makes them great as a replacement for artificial sweeteners and table sugar as a supplement for sweetness.

Generally, eating fruit as part of a healthful diet should not increase the risk of diabetes. A diet that is high in sugar, refined carbohydrates, and saturated fats is likely to be more of a risk. [...] #### Related Articles

