lly induced by apoE4, we used gene editing to generate an isogenic apoE3/3-hiPSC line from the apoE4/4-hiPSC-A line (Supplementary Fig. 6a)29. As in the parental line, the isogenic apoE3/3-hiPSC line (iE3/3) had normal expression of pluripotency genes (Supplementary Fig. 6b,c) and a normal karyotype (Supplementary Fig. 6d), and it generated normal neural stem cells, which expressed Sox2, nestin, and FoxG1
