Content: In the present study, the ERAP1 SNP rs27037 increased the risk of axSpA in individuals carrying the HLA-B27 gene. Our results are compatible with those of several studies,[40-43] which confirmed an epistatic interaction between the ERAP SNP and HLA-B27 loci, where there was aberrant trimming or presentation of the peptides. [...] ### Limitations

This study has some limitations. The main limitation of this study was its small sample size, which included a single population sampled from a solitary center. In addition, previous trials and reviews have reported that an epistatic interaction between ERAP1 SNPs and the HLA-B27 locus plays an essential role in the risk of axSpA susceptibility. However, the HLA-B27-positive cases in this study were only 46.7%.

