Content: Vascular calcification is a manifestation and indicator of atherosclerosis . Coronary artery , mitral valve  and thoracic aorta calcification  are strong risk factors for incident cardiovascular disease (CVD). Recent studies have suggested fibroblast growth factor 21 (FGF21) as a novel hormone with a potential regulatory role in vascular calcification. [...] FGF21 is a polypeptide hormone with anti-inflammatory, anti-diabetic and antioxidant effects [5,6]. Indeed, FGF21 has exhibited a cardioprotective effect in animal studies . Paradoxically, in clinical studies, elevated circulating FGF21 levels are often associated with an increased CVD risk . The elevation of FGF21 levels may be due to the presence of FGF21 resistance or compensatory responses to the underlying metabolic stress . [...] ### Atherosclerosis. (2017) 
