Title: Myeloid-derived suppressor cells in cancer: therapeutic targets to ...
URL: https://ehoonline.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s40164-024-00505-7
Content: # Myeloid-derived suppressor cells in cancer: therapeutic targets to overcome tumor immune evasion A population of distinct immature myeloid cells, myeloid-derived suppressor cells (MDSCs), mediate immune escape primarily by exerting immunosuppressive effects and participating in the constitution of an immunosuppressive microtumor environment. This review not only contributes to a systematic and comprehensive understanding of the essential role of MDSCs in immune system reactions against tumors but also provides information to guide the development of cancer therapies targeting MDSCs. Junli Lu, Yiming Luo, Dean Rao, Tiantian Wang, Zhen Lei, Xiaoping Chen, Bixiang Zhang & Wenjie Huang *et al.* Myeloid-derived suppressor cells in cancer: therapeutic targets to overcome tumor immune evasion.
