Content: Because of its key role in HSC production and the regulation of the blood cell environment, GATA3 is believed to be implicated in the development of various hematological disorders. If GATA3's activity is disrupted or dysregulated, it could lead to issues in blood cell formation or function, contributing to diseases such as leukemia or other blood-related disorders. Essentially, any alteration in GATA3's role in the hematopoietic system could disrupt normal blood cell development and function, [...] suggesting that GATA3 is necessary for maintaining normal LT-HSC numbers and regulating their entry into the cell cycle . Alternatively, employing a conditional _Gata3_ knockout mouse line crossed with a Vav-Cre line, Buza-Vidas et al. showed that deleting _Gata3_ from HSCs after their emergence in the embryo does not impact the HSCs' ability to expand normally. In addition, _Gata3_ absence does not influence the capacity of HSCs for self-renewal, and their numbers remain unaffected in the bone [...] | GATA3 | Blood | Hematopoietic stem cells, T cells (lymphoid), Treg cells (lymphoid), Innate lymphoid cells, Natural killer cells | In thymocyte development, GATA3 activates TCRα and ThPOK, promotes Th2 cytokines for Th1/Th2 differentiation, enhances forkhead box P3 (Foxp3) for regulatory T-cell (Treg) stability, and regulates RAR-related orphan receptor alpha (ROR-α) protein for innate lymphoid cell (ILC2) formation. | [24,25] | [...] marrow (BM) after birth in mice . The discrepancy in these two research findings highlights the need for further investigation to clarify GATA3's specific role in HSC regulation. Notably, Frelin et al. reported that GATA3 influences the equilibrium between the self-renewal and differentiation of LT-HSC by governing their reprogramming from LT-HSC to IT-HSC which plays a crucial role in maintaining stable blood counts. The depletion of _Gata3_ in mice elevated the repopulating capacity and the [...] initiated and acts in adult hematop