### More on Cancer

photo of more on compass

#### Understanding Cancer Basics

#### How to Spot the Early Warning Signs of Cancer [...] Your doctor will also prescribe medicine to help with stomach acid. It might include proton-pump inhibitors, H2 blockers, or bismuth subsalicylate (Bismatrol, Pepto-Bismol). This medicine also helps your antibiotics work better because it calms inflammation in your stomach.

About a month after you finish your antibiotics, your doctor can test for H. pylori to make sure it's gone. If there are still signs of the infection, you may need more antibiotics.

