d to patient characteristics, variations in treatments, and differences in assessment methods between the studies. Scapular stabilization training and shoulder mobilization/stretching showed mild improvement in short-term shoulder pain, whereas an eccentric exercise program did not have a significant effect on short-term pain, and none of the three specific exercise types improved the pain level of the reduced shoulder
