rvival and a high [...] GBM is primarily diagnosed in adults with a median age of 64 years. The incidence increases with age, peaking at 75 to 84 years and dropping after 85 years.This incidence rate among cohorts aged 65 and older has been shown to increase to 130 per million individuals.( The number of cases is expected to increase, given the increase in the aging population in the United States.It comprises almost half of the annual 24,000 new cases of primary malignant brain tumors in the US.(

