ice. [...] many groups following reperfusion therapy in both animal stroke models and AIS patients and is shown to be a major contributing factor of HT.7, 17, 18, 19, 20, 23, 49 The essential role of cerebrovascular Wnt/β‐catenin signaling in BBB formation and integrity has been well documented by us and others in animal studies. Impaired Wnt/β‐catenin signaling in mouse embryos led to severe BBB disruption and intracerebral hemorrhage by altering expressions of BBB markers Glut‐1, Claudin‐5, and
