ciation between relationship status and HIV care outcomes would vary by sexual agreement. Existing evidence indicates that sexual agreements contextualize associations between relationship status and drug use. SMM in monogamous relationships are less likely to use a wide range of illicit drugs (e.g., cocaine/crack, methamphetamine, gamma-hydroxybutyrate, ketamine, and ecstasy) compared with SMM in nonmonogamous relationships and those who are single
