### Cell Division and Differentiation

One of the key features of embryonic stem cells is their ability to divide and differentiate. But how exactly does this process work? When a stem cell divides, it can either remain a stem cell or become another type with a more specific function, like a muscle cell, a red blood cell, or a brain cell.
