ating endodermal differentiation (Assady et al., 2001). In addition, as further evidence of their pluripotency, embryonic stem cells can form embryoid bodies, which are cell aggregations that contain all three embryonic germ layers while in culture, and can form teratomas in vivo (Itskovitz-Eldor et al., 2000).
