Content: In addition to these observations with peripheral blood T cells, we found that IL-10 also inhibited directly the proliferation of a tetanus toxoid-specific CD4+ T-cell clone in the presence of immobilized OKT3 MoAb. There was no evidence for monocytes contaminating this antigen-specific clonal T-cell population, because tetanus toxoid added to the T cells failed to induce cell growth. Together, these findings demonstrate that human IL-10 can directly inhibit T-cell growth induced through CD3 [...] T-cell growth inhibition by IL-10 was reported to occur indirectly and to require the presence of monocytes.1, 12, 13, 14 When EBV-immortalized cells, rather than monocytes, were used as antigen-presenting cells, IL-10 failed to inhibit the proliferation of human CD4+ clones in response to antigen.12 Because human IL-10 was found to reduce class II MHC expression in human monocytes, but not in EBV-immortalized B cells, it was suggested that human IL-10 may inhibit antigen-specific T-cell [...] culture. IL-10 inhibited these accessory cell-dependent responses over a wide range of monocyte concentrations. In the presence of monocytes at high concentrations (20 to 50 × 103 cells per well), inhibition by IL-10 was reduced (more clearly seen with PHA). Thus, in the presence of immobilized OKT3 MoAb, where monocytes are not required to induce T-cell proliferation, IL-10 can inhibit T-cell growth. [...] In the presence of monocytes, IL-10 inhibits IL-2 production by activated T cells.11 To assess whether this inhibitory effect of IL-10 requires the presence of monocytes, highly purified peripheral blood T cells were stimulated with immobilized OKT3 with or without IL-10. In three experiments (Table 3), IL-10 inhibited IL-2 secretion induced by immobilized OKT3 MoAb by a mean of 51.5% in the absence of added monocytes. In the presence of monocyte-enriched populations, IL-10 inhibited IL-2 [...] Table 1. IL-10 Directly Inhibits the Proliferation of CD4+ T Cells

