Title: Effects of beta-blockers for congestive heart failure in ...
URL: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25283168/
Content: Conclusion:
Beta-blocker therapy was associated with a significant improvement of echocardiographic parameters in patients with systemic LV failure. However, the use of beta-blockers did not provide significant benefits in terms of improving the EF in patients with RV failure. Nonetheless, beta-blockers may be effective to prevent the clinical deterioration of pediatric and CHD patients with heart failure.

