Content: #### Figure 2. Associations between systolic blood pressure (SBP), diastolic blood pressure (DBP), pulse pressure (PP) and risk of abdominal aortic aneurysm or thoracic abdominal aneurysm. HR indicates the relative risk increases with per-SD higher blood pressure. Models were adjusted for assessment centres, age, sex, race, tertiles of deprivation index, smoking status, alcohol consumption frequency, BMI, genetic diseases, HbA1c, cholesterol and HDL-C. For PP and DBP, the models were [...] ### Conclusions

Elevated DBP and reduced PP, but not SBP, were independently associated with a higher risk of incident AA, highlighting their potential to refine clinical risk stratification.

