induced neurons found [...] of LRRK2 filaments and rescued axonal transport . Mechanistically, it seems plausible that the impairment of mitochondrial transport observed in this study represents a non-specific disruption of axonal transport by the formation of LRRK2 filaments around microtubules, rather than a specific effect on mitochondrial transport. The finding that overexpression of LRRK2-p.R1441C and LRRK2-p.Y1699C, but not LRRK2-p.G2019S, caused transport impairment is consistent with this idea, since the p.R1441C
