Content: Leucine-rich repeat kinase 2 (LRRK2) is a large, multi-domain kinase whose mutations have been associated with the development of familial and sporadic Parkinson’s disease (PD), but also with an increased susceptibility to leprosy, Crohn’s disease, and several forms of cancer (Bae and Lee, 2015, Cogo et al., 2017, Lebovitz et al., 2021, Saunders-Pullman et al., 2010). In addition, LRRK2 expression levels have been recently shown to influence survival in progressive supranuclear palsy (Jabbari [...] Special issue articles Recommended articles

