Content: Signal peptide peptidase (SPP) is defined as an aspartyl intramembrane-cleaving protease that is part of the GxGD protease family, involved in the regulated intramembrane proteolysis of single span transmembrane proteins. SPP is closely related to the γ-secretase complex and its homologues, the signal peptide peptidase-like proteases (SPPLs).

