Title: Signal peptide peptidase functions in ERAD to cleave the unfolded ...
URL: https://www.embopress.org/doi/10.15252/embj.201488208
Content: Synopsis

Image 25: image

Signal peptide peptidase (SPP), an intramembrane protease involved in ER signal peptide cleavage, functions in a previously unrecognized ERAD branch, catalyzing proteolysis of the unfolded protein response (UPR) regulator XPB 1u in complex with Derlin1 and TRC 8.

