Content: The MICALs are a family of actin-regulatory oxidation–reduction (redox) enzymes that directly bind and disassemble actin filaments (F-actin) . Three vertebrate MICAL genes, MICAL-1, -2 and -3, and one Drosophila Mical gene have been identified and are collectively called the MICALs.
