timulatory pathway is required for optimal T cell activation and therefore has been implicated in the induction and progression of autoimmune diseases, it is also required for the generation and the homeostasis of Treg cells. Several studies performed in mice showed that CD28 inhibition led to a reduction in Treg cell number with important implications for allograft rejection (74). Moreover, CD28-deficient Treg cells expressed low levels of CTLA-4, PD-1, and C-C chemokine receptor type 6,
