Semaglutide, a long-acting GLP-1 analog with the addition of a C18 fatty diacid resulting in an extended half-life of 165​hours, was approved for obesity management at a subcutaneous dose of 2.4​mg weekly. Semaglutide is also approved for T2D treatment at a dose of up to 1.0​mg weekly subcutaneously, and as an oral formulation at a dose of 7 and 14​mg daily. [...] . Most of these are based on replicating (or inhibiting) the action of one or more gut-derived hormones, including GLP-1, GIP, amylin and glucagon. Early-phase clinical trials are reporting unprecedented weight loss and glycaemic improvements for several of these agents, approaching the results achievable with bariatric surgery, at least in the short-term.

