wever, three [...] stroke in the presence of vascular risk factors, several studies have shown that the association between migraine and ischaemic stroke is apparent in people with low Framingham Risk Score.39 40 42 The few exceptions were a positive association with family history of cardiovascular disease, cigarette smoking and oral contraceptives.42 This agrees with reports that coronary and carotid arteries of individuals with active migraine are found to be less severely affected by atherosclerosis than
