or of [...] Reiter’s laboratory has developed the foundation on which to realize anti-N-cadherin therapy for patients. In a seminal paper published in Nature Medicine, Dr. Reiter’s group demonstrated that their antibodies could slow growth of prostate cancer xenografts, block invasion and metastasis, and at high doses, allow complete regression in vivo. N-cadherin expression is positively correlated to progression in bladder cancer, a disease that claims nearly 75,000 lives annually in the U.S. Dr.
