Content: A novel method that permits a high-resolution, quantitative analysis of replication fork initiation, progression and termination has been recently developed in _Saccharomyces cerevisiae_27.""),28.""). The principle is to isolate and sequence Okazaki fragments to reveal the proportions of rightward- (_R_) and leftward- (_L_) moving forks throughout the genome. Zones of predominant initiation (termination) can then be detected as upward (downward) slopes in replication fork directionality [...] Full size image

