Introduction

Non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs) are generally the preferred agents in currently recommended combinations for the treatment of HIV-1 infection. Although there are three NNRTIs approved by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA), efavirenz (EFV), delavirdine (DLV) and nevirapine (NVP), only EFV and NVP are licensed for use in the UK and Europe.
