Background [...] Conclusion

It is imperative to recognize the factors that are associated with NPPV success in lung transplant recipients presenting with respiratory failure, as NPPV failure and need for IMV portends worse outcomes. Overall, the results of this study suggest that NPPV is a viable option for lung transplant recipients with acute respiratory failure. It should be instituted with extreme caution, however, in recipients with high severity of illness and/or severe hypoxemia. [...] •Lung transplant recipients with acute respiratory failure are at high risk of death. 
