rnitine [...] additional mechanisms, and which specific microbial species contribute to TMAO formation, have not been fully clarified. l-carnitine is an abundant nutrient in red meat and contains a trimethylamine structure similar to that of choline (Fig. 1a). Although dietary ingestion is a major source of l-carnitine in omnivores, it is also endogenously produced in mammals from lysine and serves an essential function in transporting fatty acids into the mitochondrial compartment10, 11. l-Carnitine
