Content: A stable partnership seems to slow progression to AIDS or death for patients receiving highly active antiretroviral treatment (HAART), a Swiss cohort study has shown. Exactly how such partnerships might affect outcome is purely speculative but warrants further study, especially of the mechanisms suitable for intervention, say its authors.

