Title: α+-thalassaemia and malarial anaemia - ScienceDirect.com
URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1471492208002043
Content: The mechanisms by which α+-thalassaemia protects against severe malaria, and severe malarial anaemia in particular, are poorly understood. A recent report proposes that the increased count of microcytic and hypochromic erythrocytes in α+-thalassaemia reduces the haemoglobin decline during acute malaria and, thus, reduces the risk of anaemia. This mechanism might add to further α+-thalassaemic attributes that are involved in the attenuation of anaemia caused by both acute and chronic [...] α+-thalassaemia, which is usually caused by deletions within the α-globin gene cluster, is an extremely common erythrocyte variant of humans that reaches prevalences of >60% in Africa and even higher in parts of Asia and Oceania 1, 2, 3. α+-thalassaemia is characterized by microcytosis (see Glossary), and reduced overall and erythrocytic haemoglobin (Hb) concentrations, in addition to an increased erythrocyte count; these changes are more pronounced (but still mild) in homozygous individuals [...] without malaria, those with mixed _Plasmodium_ infection were at greatest risk of severe anemia (adjusted odds ratio [AOR] 3.25 [95% CI 2.99–3.54]); AORs for severe anaemia associated with _P. falciparum_, _P. vivax_, and _P. malariae_ were 2.11 (95% CI 2.00–2.23), 1.87 (95% CI 1.74–2.01), and 2.18 (95% CI 1.76–2.67), respectively, _p_<0.001. Overall, 12.2% (95% CI 11.2%–13.3%) of severe anemia was attributable to non-falciparum infections compared with 15.1% (95% CI 13.9%–16.3%) for _P. [...] Fowkes _et al._ do not ultimately unravel the puzzle of α+-thalassaemic protection but propose a mechanism by which the degree of anaemia that follows acute malaria is attenuated. In fact, the increased count of microcytic erythrocytes in α+-thalassaemia might be responsible for a milder presentation of acute malarial anaemia. Such a mechanism should also be present in other traits with an increased microerythrocyte count but, as with α+-thalassaemia, it could prove difficult to dissect the [...] Microcytosis and more
