### Authors

Debra L Weiner1,Patricia L Hibberd,Peter Betit,Andrew B Cooper,Christine A Botelho,Carlo Brugnara [...] Objective: To explore the efficacy and safety of inhaled nitric oxide (INO) for treatment of vaso-occlusive crisis in pediatric patients.

Design: Prospective, double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized clinical trial with enrollment between September 1999 and October 2001.

Setting: Urban, tertiary care children's hospital in the United States.

Participants: Twenty patients aged 10 to 21 years with sickle cell disease and severe acute vaso-occlusive crisis. [...] Intervention: Patients were randomly assigned to receive INO (80 ppm with 21% final concentration of inspired oxygen; n = 10), or placebo (21% inspired oxygen; n = 10) for 4 hours. [...] Conclusions: Results of this exploratory study suggest that INO may be beneficial for acute vaso-occlusive crisis. These preliminary results warrant further investigation.

