ith DNA damage accumulation (Zeman & Cimprich, 2014). Our previous work (Zimmer _et al_, 2016) demonstrated that treatment with pyridostatin slows down replication fork progression in BRCA2‐deficient cells, suggesting that G4s stabilised by pyridostatin assemble persistent DNA secondary structures that obstruct replication. BRCA2 has a central role in protecting stalled replication forks against nucleolytic degradation, illustrated by extensive
