Content: The number of TCSs differs enormously from species to species and seems to correlate with the variety of environmental cues bacteria are exposed to. It ranges from 0 in _Mycoplasma genitalium_, over 30/32 (HKs/RRs) in _Escherichia coli_, 36/34 in _Bacillus subtilis_, to 131/80 in _Anabaena_ sp. strain PCC7120, and 132/119 in _Myxococcus xanthus_ . [...] TCSs in branched phosphotransfer pathways [...] Most of the TCSs seem to be specific in their phosphotransfer reactions, and cross-talk seems to be rather the exception . Since bacteria are exposed to different gradients of environmental signals, it is well conceivable that TCSs are interconnected [47•]. Acid stress adaptation provides a good example for the interconnectivity of several TCSs (Figure 3) [34••]. Low pH activates the EvgS/EvgA system, which induces the YdeO/GadE cascade. In addition, _safA_ is induced. The connector SafA [...] reactions (Figure 1). Besides TCSs with a single phosphotransfer step, phosphorelays are known, which allow multiple phosphotransfer reactions (Figure 1). TCSs are widely distributed throughout the prokaryotic and eukaryotic kingdoms, with the exception of mammals, making them an interesting target for novel antimicrobials. [...] J.S. Parkinson _et al._
