s [...] Considering the overall results, adding scapular therapeutic exercises to the experimental group intervention was significantly more effective than the control group interventions (SMD = 0.52 [95%Cl: 0.05, 0.99], P = .03, I2 = 76%, 323 patients total) (Fig. 4). Despite the large heterogeneity, the results were associated with a moderate effect size.

