nvolvement in [...] LS mutants have been reported to affect the activation of the PI3K/Akt/mTOR and MAPK pathways in different biological systems (12–16, 18). Consistently, in our study, we observed that expression of the T468M mutant of SHP2 resulted in insulin-evoked PI3K/Akt and MAPK pathway hyperactivation in several metabolic tissues. Therefore, we assessed the impact of chronic inhibition of those pathways on the metabolic phenotype of LS mice. To this aim, we treated 25-wk-old LS and WT animals for 1 mo
