ing in brain results in a cell fate shift resulting in imbalance of cell types in central nervous system with more neurons and less astrocytes in the hippocampus and cortex (Gauthier et al., 2007). The SHP2-D61G and, to a lesser extent, SHP2-N308D mouse model display spatial learning and memory deficits, due to enhanced RAS/MAPK signaling, which enhances excitatory synaptic function and
