n the [...] _Bacillus subtilis_ serves as a model for motility of Gram-positive bacteria. _B.subtilis_ has three described mechanisms of motility: swimming, swarming, and sliding (25–29). Swimming and swarming motility are driven by the action of flagella, which provide propulsion to the bacteria. Swimming _B.subtilis_ use multiple, peritrichous flagella to move as single cells through aqueous media. When the surrounding medium is sufficiently viscous, _B.subtilis_ cells join into rafts that use swarming
