 rights and content

Highlights [...] connections, and the interactions between Van Gogh bundles and other phenotypic cells are confined to a specific region (repulsive inside the region, attractive outside it). In a single-biofilm system, as nutrients are depleted, increasing numbers of motile cells transform into matrix-producing cells, forming Van Gogh bundles that guide the biofilm expansion towards areas with higher nutrient concentrations, thereby enhancing its expansion ability. In a muti-biofilm system, extreme nutrient [...] Our study, by means of experiment and simulation, shows the significant role of Van Gogh bundles in _Bacillus subtilis_ biofilm expansion. These bundles, formed after cell differentiation, coordinate with other phenotypic cells to direct biofilm growth toward nutrient-rich areas. In one biofilm system, the lack of nutrients induces the transformation of motile cells into matrix-producing cells, forming Van Gogh bundles that guide biofilm expansion. In multi-biofilm system, nutrient depletion [...] •Motile cells transform into matrix-producing cell under nutrient-deficient environments. 
   •Cell chains composed of matrix-producing cells form Van Gogh bundles by bending and folding. 
   •The synergistic effect of Van Gogh bundles and other phenotypic cells promotes the expansion of Bacillus subtilis biofilms 
   •Van gogh bundles as the emergent structure give biofilms extra ecological advantages. 

