Kempen J, Newcomb C, Washington T, et al. Ophthalmology, December 2023 [...] ## Limitations

While the study did show that over a median of 10 years these agents did not increase overall or cancer-related mortality, there is evidence that longer-term or lifelong use of immunosuppressive therapy, such as in the case of transplant patients, is associated with an increased risk of mortality. This study of patients with OID did not look at usage beyond a median of 10 years. Additionally, the findings may not be applicable for less commonly used immunosuppressants. [...] ## Limitations

