Title: The role of transmembrane protein 27 (TMEM27) in islet physiology ...
URL: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20386877/
Content: Abstract

Aims/hypothesis: Transmembrane protein 27 (TMEM27) is a membrane protein cleaved and shed by pancreatic beta cells that has been proposed as a beta cell mass biomarker. Despite reports of its possible role in insulin exocytosis and cell proliferation, its function in beta cells remains controversial. We aimed to characterise the function of TMEM27 in islets and its potential use as a beta cell mass biomarker. [...] Conclusions/interpretation: Our data support a role for TMEM27 in glucose-induced insulin secretion but not in cell proliferation. The finding that its cleavage is not specific to beta cells challenges the current support for its use as a potential beta cell mass biomarker.

