Title: TNFAIP3 affects ferroptosis after traumatic brain injury by affecting ...
URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0891584924011572
Content: The TNFAIP3 gene encodes a protein called TNFAIP3 (tumor necrosis factor-α-induced protein 3) . This protein, which is also known as A20, is an inhibitory protein in cells that plays a role in regulating immune and inflammatory responses [13,14]. By various means, it regulates the signaling pathways that affect protein modification and thereby limits the reaction of cells to inflammatory signals [13,14]. The main functions of A20 include negative regulation of the TNF signaling pathway through [...] deubiquitination (removal of ubiquitin tags) and inhibition of the connections between key signaling molecules . It can also regulate immune and inflammatory responses by inhibiting the NF-kB signaling pathway. It can also affect the expression of cell apoptosis-related proteins and regulate cell apoptosis processes. Abnormal expression or mutation of TNFAIP3 is associated with the development of various diseases, including inflammatory and autoimmune diseases and certain types of cancer [...] (sc-166374, mouse monoclonal, 1:1000; Santa Cruz), or NEDD4 (5344, rabbit monoclonal, 1:1000; Cell Signaling Technology). After incubation with secondary antibodies conjugated to horseradish peroxidase (BeoTech Company, China, A0208, A0216, 1:5000) for 2 h, the protein bands were visualized using a chemiluminescence ECL kit (Beyotime Biotechnology, Beijing, China). [...] blocking with 5% bovine serum albumin in PBS at 37°C for 1 h. The sections were then incubated overnight at 4°C with specific primary antibodies, washed three times with PBS, and incubated with Alexa Fluor 488- or CytM3-conjugated secondary antibodies (Jackson, USA; 1:500) at 37°C for 1 h. After washing with PBS, DAPI nuclear staining (Abcam, ab104139) was performed at room temperature. Immunofluorescence images were acquired using a laser scanning confocal microscope (TCS SP5II, Leica, [...] Cell viability was assessed using a Cell Counting Kit-8 (CCK-8, CK04, Dojindo, Tokyo, Japan) as previously described . Briefly, the cells were cultured in 96-well plates, and the plates were incubated at 37°C for 2 h after addition of the reagent. The optical density (OD) of each well at 450 nm was then measured using a Thermo Multiskan FC microplate reader. To quantify cell damage-induced cytotoxicity, a cell toxicity detection kit (Beyotime Biotech, China) was used. Following the
