Content: Tumor necrosis factor, alpha-induced protein 3 (TNFAIP3) is a gene that encodes a protein that functions as a zinc finger protein and ubiquitin-editing enzyme. The protein inhibits NF-kappa B activation and TNF-mediated apoptotic death. Missense mutations, nonsense mutations, silent mutations, whole gene deletions, frameshift deletions and insertions, and in-frame deletions are observed in cancers such as hematopoietic and lymphoid cancers, intestinal cancer, and stomach cancer. [...] Vanderbilt-Ingram Cancer CenterCopyright © 2010 - 2017 MY CANCER GENOME [...] Immune checkpoints

