URL: https://aacrjournals.org/cancerres/article/66/8_Supplement/925/530307/Alpha-tocopherol-does-not-protect-against-prostate
Content: The notion that vitamin E can prevent prostate cancer is primarily derived from the ABCT study where a low (50 mg/day) dose of α-tocopherol reduced prostate cancer risk in smokers. This study forms the basis for the ongoing SELECT study in which the effect of a 400 mg/day dose of α-tocopherol is being tested. Most epidemiologic studies in non-smokers do not support a preventive effect of vitamin E against prostate cancer. In previous animal studies, no preventive effects were found, but these [...] Maarten C. Bosland, Lori Horton, Sally Lasano; Alpha-tocopherol does not protect against prostate cancer but promotes mammary cancer in male NBL rats treated with testosterone and estradiol-17-beta. _\\_Cancer Res\\__ 15 April 2006; 66 (8_Supplement): 925–926.

