Abstract

Objective: To evaluate the effects of the Diabetes Education and Self-Management for Ongoing and Newly Diagnosed (DESMOND) program on patient activation in adults living with type 2 diabetes (T2D). [...] Practice implications: In line with international diabetes guidelines it is recommended that people living with T2D, particularly those with lower levels of activation, attend an evidence based DSME such as DESMOND to increase their capacity to effectively self-manage their condition.

Keywords: Diabetes education; Patient activation; Patient self-management; Type 2 diabetes mellitus.

