Title: National Obesity Awareness Week: Find out if self- ...
URL: https://www.desmond.nhs.uk/news-articles/national-obesity-awareness-week-find-out-if-self-management-education-programmes-can-help
Content: Established in 2003, DESMOND is a group-based type 2 diabetes self-management programme which was developed by a multi-disciplinary team from across the UK and now with its Head Office here at LDC. DESMOND is currently commissioned in over 100 areas in the UK and Ireland as the type 2 diabetes patient education of choice.

   In 2022-23 46.5% of all goals set by patients attending a DESMOND group were linked to weight loss4 [...] Our data shows that 52.6% of MyDESMOND users who were classified as overweight or obese when they started using MyDESMOND lost >5% of their body weight after 6-months or more use6

   Whilst 66% of all users reported they were more active and 79% reported changes to their diet as result of using MyDESMOND4

Let’s Prevent Diabetes [...] Let’s Prevent Diabetes is a group education programme that aims to support people identified as at higher risk for developing type 2 diabetes to prevent or delay the condition.. A digital version is also available on the MyDESMOND platform.

The lifestyle changes supported by this programme have helped many of the attendees to lose weight. [...] Our original 2008 trial for people newly diagnosed with type 2 diabetes was associated with benefits in weight loss, illness beliefs, physical activity, smoking status and depression5.

MyDESMOND

MyDESMOND is the online version of the award-winning DESMOND group programme. MyDESMOND’s portable, interactive, web-based platform supports people with type 2 diabetes to manage their health. The programme has helped over 53,000 users since its launch in 2018. [...] Obesity is complex with potentially multiple causes. Obesity and overweight occurs when extra calories are stored in the body as fat. A balanced diet and active lifestyle can help support weight care, as well as in managing type 2 diabetes. Over many years here at LDC we have developed a range of education programmes designed to support people to self-manage their health; read on to find out the impact these have had directly on supporting people’s weight care journeys.

