Content: The structured “Diabetes Education and Self-Management for Ongoing and Newly Diagnosed” (DESMOND) program is a group education program with a structured curriculum and underpinned by multiple learning theories. It has previously been shown to improve biomedical, psychosocial and lifestyle outcomes [7,9,10]. A large-scale (n = 824) cluster randomized controlled trial of DESMOND demonstrated that at one year follow up DESMOND participants had (i) greater understanding of their diabetes, (ii) [...] Access through your organization

