e [...] In the last few years, several non-adrenergic mechanisms have been shown to induce WAT browning and BAT activation via molecules arising from the liver, skeletal muscle, and even heart (Villarroya and Vidal-Puig, 2013). It is not yet known whether M2 macrophages can secrete any of these molecules. Reitman (2017) specifically addressed this point and listed more than twenty putative candidates. Granneman and collaborators proposed that M2 macrophages promote the browning of adipose tissue
