Content: _Saccharomyces cerevisiae_ is a eukaryotic model used to study a plethora of biological processes. Also, _S. cerevisiae_ maintains a highly conserved AMPK signaling pathway . The orthologous signaling pathway of AMPK in _S. cerevisiae_ is composed of three upstream kinases (Elm1p, Tos3p, and Sak1p) that regulate the SNF1 complex, comprised of Snf1p, the catalytic alpha unit, two catalytic regulatory proteins, gamma (Snf4p), and beta (Sip1p, Sip2p, and Gal83p). Indeed, _S. cerevisiae_ presents [...] Overall, these results indicate that the SNF1 pathway regulates the exponential growth of _S. cerevisiae,_ mainly influenced by glucose concentration. [...] 35.Madrigal-Perez LA, Canizal-Garcia M, Gonzalez-Hernandez JC, Reynoso-Camacho R, Nava GM, Ramos-Gomez M. Energy-dependent effects of resveratrol in Saccharomyces cerevisiae. Yeast. 2016;33:227–234. doi: 10.1002/yea.3158. [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar] [...] 29.Carrillo-Garmendia A, Martinez-Ortiz C, Martinez-Garfias JG, Suarez-Sandoval SE, González-Hernández JC, Nava GM, et al. Snf1p/Hxk2p/Mig1p pathway regulates hexose transporters transcript levels, affecting the exponential growth and mitochondrial respiration of Saccharomyces cerevisiae. Fungal Gene Biol : FG & B. 2022;161:103701. doi: 10.1016/j.fgb.2022.103701. [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar] [...] AMPK can act as a tumor suppressor . AMPK activation by energy or nutrients lacking promotes inhibition of cellular growth to economize ATP . On the contrary, dysregulation of the AMPK pathway induces a metabolic reprogramming associated with cancer via LKB1 protein  or MAGE-A3/6 . Nonetheless, how the AMPK pathway regulates growth is poorly understood. In _S. cerevisiae_, Snf1p has a key role in maintaining growth under non-fermentative conditions, using non-fermentable carbon sources or
Score: 0.6882385


