Abstract

Objective: To investigate the risks of attempted and completed suicide in women who experienced a stillbirth, miscarriage, or termination of pregnancy within 1 year postnatally and compare this risk with that in women who experienced a live birth.

Design: A nested case-control study. [...] Conclusions: The risk of suicide might increase in women who experience fetal loss within 1 year postnatally. Healthcare professionals and family members should enhance their sensitivity to care for possible mental distress, particularly for women who have experienced a stillbirth.

Tweetable abstract: Suicide risk increased in women who had a stillbirth, miscarriage, or termination of pregnancy within 1 year postnatally. [...] Factors influencing attempted and completed suicide in postnatal women: A population-based study in Taiwan.Weng SC, Chang JC, Yeh MK, Wang SM, Chen YH.Weng SC, et al.Sci Rep. 2016 May 12;6:25770. doi: 10.1038/srep25770.Sci Rep. 2016.PMID: 27173845 Free PMC article. [...] termination of pregnancy (aOR 2.5; 95% CI 1.63-3.82). In addition to marital and educational statuses, psychological illness increased the risk of suicidal behaviour.
