Content: The team also explain that women who were already experiencing symptoms of post-traumatic stress and depression may have been more likely to respond to the questionnaire, which could mean the number of women suffering psychological symptoms may appear higher. [...] The study revealed that one month following pregnancy loss, nearly a third of women (29 per cent) suffered post-traumatic stress while one in four (24 per cent) experienced moderate to severe anxiety, and one in ten (11 per cent) had moderate to severe depression.

Nine months later, 18 per cent of women had post-traumatic stress, 17 per cent moderate to severe anxiety, and 6 per cent had moderate to severe depression.

Access to treatment [...] Image 3
One in six women experience long-term post-traumatic stress following miscarriage or ectopic pregnancy.

This is the finding of the largest ever study31369-9/fulltext) into the psychological impact of early-stage pregnancy loss, from scientists at Imperial College London and KU Leuvenin Belgium.

> Pregnancy loss affects up to one in two women, and for many women it will be the most traumatic event in their life.Professor Tom BourneStudy author [...] However, they add that the fact that such a large proportion were experiencing symptoms suggests many women could be suffering in silence. Dr Jessica Farren, first author of the research from Imperial, and Obstetrician and Gynaecologist, said: “Post-traumatic stress can have a toxic effect on all elements of a person’s life – affecting work, home and relationships.” [...] Daily Mail: “Women reveal the true effect of their heartbreaking loss as study finds one in six will develop PTSD”Grazia: “I Had PTSD After My Miscarriage - And So Do 30 percent Of Women Who Have Had Miscarriages”The Times: “Third of women have PTSD after losing baby through miscarriage or ectopic pregnancy”Independent: “One in six women suffer from PTSD symptoms a year after miscarriage or ectopic pregnancy, study finds”BBC News: “ Miscarriage can lead to 'long-term post-traumatic stress'”ITV
