Title: How to Manage (or Prevent) Semaglutide Side Effects
URL: https://www.medpartnerstl.com/post/how-to-manage-or-prevent-semaglutide-side-effects
Content: Nausea is the most common side effect. You may overcome nausea and other gastrointestinal side effects if you:

 Eat slowly
 Eat smaller portions
 Eat bland, low-fat foods (crackers, rice, and toast)
 Eat foods like soup that are high in water
 Drink clear beverages (water, ginger ale, clear broth, tea, and sports drinks)
 Avoid greasy, fried foods
 Don’t lie down right after eating

Over-the-counter medications for gas, diarrhea, and heartburn can also help. [...] The most common side effects caused by semaglutide-containing medications include:

 Nausea
 Vomiting
 Diarrhea
 Abdominal pain
 Constipation
 Headache
 Dizziness
 Abdominal bloating (excessive gas)

People metabolize medications differently, so there’s no way to predict side effects. However, the risk is often associated with the dose. The higher the dose, the more likely these side effects.

### Facial drooping [...] Semaglutide is the active ingredient in Ozempic®, Wegovy®, and Rybelsus®. These innovative weight loss medications have transformed the lives of millions of Americans.

Like all medications, semaglutide can cause side effects. Most of these problems affect your gastrointestinal system and disappear as your body adjusts to the medicine. But you don’t need to wait it out. [...] Preventing side effects begins with prescribing a low dose and gradually increasing the amount in each injection. This approach often prevents side effects by allowing your body to adjust to the medicine slowly.

If gastrointestinal problems develop, they usually disappear in a few weeks when your body gets used to semaglutide. We can also help decrease your uncomfortable symptoms by readjusting your medication regimen as needed. [...] Serious side effects range from pancreatitis and kidney disease to low blood sugar and vision changes. In some cases, people have serious side effects because they have a health problem that increases their risk.

Sometimes, conditions develop without a known risk factor. However, more research is needed to determine whether starting semaglutide is connected.
