Title: Granulomas: What Is It, Types, Causes, and More | Osmosis
URL: https://www.osmosis.org/answers/granulomas
Content: Granulomas: What Is It, Types, Causes, and More | Osmosis Granulomas ### What is a granuloma? ### What are the types of granulomas? ### What causes granulomas to form? Granulomas form in response to chronic inflammation. Noncaseating granulomas may be formed by an inflammatory condition (e.g., sarcoidosis and Crohn disease), vasculitis, and exposure to foreign objects. ### How do granulomas form? Granulomas form when the immune system responds to the causative agents (e.g., infections and foreign objects). Prior to receiving therapy, individuals will often be tested for active TB, as TB stored within the granuloma can be released when treated with anti-TNF medications, causing a disseminated infection. Caseating granulomas are often caused by infections, while the non-caseating type is typically caused by an inflammatory condition. Granuloma.
