Fast twitch muscles help with sudden bursts of energy involved in activities like sprinting and jumping. Slow twitch muscles are better for long-term…

Muscle fibers can be found in skeletal, cardiac, and smooth muscles, and work to do different things in the body.

Climbing the StairMaster for 45 minutes is a recent social media trend. I tried this for one week and will share my experience below. [...] Let’s take a closer look at the ways slow-twitch muscles differ from fast-twitch muscles:

To visualize the differences, think of slow-twitch muscles as “plugged in” to the heart. On the other hand, fast-twitch muscles mainly run on a “battery.”

### Muscle fiber type 2a

One kind of fast-twitch muscle fiber can also act like a slow-twitch muscle fiber. It’s also called an intermediate muscle fiber or type 2a.
