"Trans-acting factors, such as lncRNAs, influence mRNA translation.",1,"Title: lncRNAs: the unexpected link between protein synthesis and cancer ...
URL: https://molecular-cancer.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s12943-025-02236-7
Content: LncRNAs can affect the secondary structures of mRNA, in particular of their 5’UTR, either promoting or hindering the binding of translation initiation factors or modifying the ribosomal scanning process. In addition, lncRNAs can influence the interaction of the mRNA cap structure and/or poly(A) tail , or of their associated proteins, with the translational machinery, enhancing or inhibiting their translation. [...] LncRNAs can also function as scaffolds to facilitate or impede the assembly of functional protein complexes, including translation initiation factors, RNA-binding proteins, and regulatory enzymes. By sequestering these factors and preventing their association with ribosomes or mRNAs, lncRNAs can reduce global or specific mRNA translation. [...] Besides, export to the cytoplasm represents an additional level of regulation of mRNA translation by affecting the accessibility of transcripts to the translational machinery. While functional evidence is still lacking, we may speculate that lncRNAs affect mRNAs cytoplasmic localization starting by controlling their nuclear retention and/or export. For example, lncRNAs can act as scaffolds for the assembly of protein complexes that are responsible for mRNA transport. Some lncRNAs exhibit [...] lncRNAs also have active roles in alternative splicing and/or polyadenylation of mRNAs, both through RNA:DNA and RNA:RNA binding capacity, which subsequently reflects on the translation of target mRNAs . Alternative splicing can lead to changes in the open reading frame (ORF), introduce premature termination codons, triggering nonsense-mediated decay (NMD) and regulating gene expression by modulating the abundance of specific mRNA isoforms, with important consequences on proteome diversity. [...] prioritize the translation of factors necessary for overcoming the stress and ensuring survival . LncRNAs actively participate in the formation and condensation of such granules, helping in the localization of mRNAs to areas where translation is either repressed or re-activated in response to specific signals, which is particularly important for cell plasticity and overcoming stress in cancer .
