Content: The mRNA encodes in principle for one protein, but its sequence also contains information to regulate the initiation of its translation. This regulatory information is usually localized in the untranslated regions (UTRs) and sometimes in the coding sequences. This information consists of short sequence motifs, base modifications, or RNAsecondary structures (Fig.2).

