2.   Download: Download full-size image [...] them being a critical parameter. Internal Ribosome Entry Sites are RNA secondary structures that can recruit a pre-initiation complex or even sometimes an 80S ribosome with variable involvement of IRES _trans_-acting factors (ITAFs). Some RNA motifs can also interact with long non-coding RNAs (lncRNA) and modulate start-codon accessibility). Finally, the start-codon nucleotide environment is also a determining factor for its selection by the ribosome as an initiation site. Both flanking [...] One example is the translation of the mRNA coding for the transcription factor ATF4, which is responsible for the transcription of genes involved in the regulation of amino acid metabolism . ATF4 is also required for resistance to oxidative stress and is essential to the coordination of the response to misfolded proteins. The set of genes activated by ATF4 constitutes the next steps of the integrated stress response. The translation regulation of the ATF4 mRNA involves a set of uORFs coupled [...] ### 3.2. The integrated stress response (ISR) [...] Most of the molecular mechanisms involved in translation regulation are linked to signaling pathways of which some translation initiation, elongation or termination factors are targets (Fig.1). Translation is therefore directly connected to environmental changes sensed by the cell. The direct impact of these signals at the translational level allows translation switches that lead to the rapid synthesis of a new set of proteins that orchestrates the cell's adaptive response to these changes.
