ds were vascularized by [...] One study that deserves special attention transplanted fetal-derived glial precursors into neonatal immunodeficient mice and found human glia throughout the entire brain within 12–20 months and was organized in a laminar structure, a phenotype previously thought to be present only in humans and nonhuman primates . The human astrocytes maintained a human astrocyte morphology (i.e., larger nuclei, long projections) within the mouse brain. Functionally, human astrocytes propagated calcium waves
