Content: Neonatal glial replacement delays disease progression in mouse models of Huntington's disease (HD), in which glial dysfunction is prominent. Here, we ask if transplanting human glial progenitor cells (hGPCs) into adult R6/2 HD mice can ameliorate the phenotype, and how diseased host neurons are affected by healthy glia. We find that the introduction of hGPCs into the striata of adult R6/2 HD mice indeed slows their motor and cognitive decline and extends survival. Single-nucleus RNA sequencing [...] PMID: 40503942
