### Step 7: Advance Needle Into the Vein

Once you receive flashback avoid the temptation to advance the needle right away, first reduce your needle angle and under ultrasound guidance advance the needle until it is centered in the lumen. [...] As you slowly proceed the needle under ultrasound guidance, you will notice some Tenting that occurs on the anterior portion of the vessel. At this point you will want to decrease the angle between the skin and the needle from 45 degrees to about 20 degrees. This will ensure that when additional pressure is applied to penetrate the anterior wall of the vein, the residual force will not puncture the posterior wall.

