e TNBC tumor growth. [...] Concurrently, an analysis predicated on two markers of T-cell activation, CD69 and CD25, revealed a substantial augmentation in the proportion of activated CD8 T cells within the tumor, along with a notable escalation in the concentration of cytokines in the interstitial fluid of the tumor. This analysis also demonstrated the merits of a minimal systemic toxic response and a paucity of therapeutic side effects [107:216.""), 108]. Specifically, V9302 has been shown to promote cancer cell
