The puncturing device, consisting of the VgrG trimer, is located at the top of the inner tube and may be crucial for piercing the prey cell envelope. The VgrG trimer sometimes terminates with a Pro-Ala-Ala-Arg (PAAR)-repeat-containing protein, sharpening the tip (Shneider et al., 2013; Bondage et al., 2016). [...] The T6SS baseplate complex, composed of TssA, TssE, TssF, TssG, TssK, and Valine-glycine repeat protein G (VgrG or TssI) proteins (Brunet et al., 2015), is recruited by the membrane complex (Zoued et al., 2013). This structure serves as a platform for contractile sheath assembly and is essential for the correct assembly of the inner tube, comprised of hexameric rings of Hemolysin-coregulated protein (Hcp or TssD) (Brunet et al., 2015). TssA forms a dodecamer complex, which first binds to the [...] Brunet, Y. R., Zoued, A., Boyer, F., Douzi, B., and Cascales, E. (2015). The type VI secretion TssEFGK-VgrG phage-like baseplate is recruited to the TssJLM membrane complex via multiple contacts and serves as assembly platform for tail tube/sheath polymerization. PLoS Genet. 11:e1005545. doi: 10.1371/journal.pgen.1005545

