Content: The VgrG trimer is 185 Å in overall length and comprises a funnel-like structure with a 35-Å-diameter lumen tapering down to a spike-like needle at the bottom (Figure 6A). Each monomer consists of seven α helices and 46 β sheets, comprising three main regions: the N-terminal head and C-terminal spike, linked together by the neck region containing a typical OB-fold motif (Figures 6B and 6C). In the neck region, each chain intertwines with the other two chains (Figure 6D). Extensive hydrophobic [...] polymerizes around it in a high-energy, extended conformation.16,17 Contraction of the sheath propels the Hcp tube, sharpened by a VgrG-PAAR spike, through the baseplate and into a neighboring cell. Diverse effector proteins are delivered attached to VgrG, PAAR, or loaded into the Hcp tube.13,18 The effector cargo may be attached via specific interactions, which may require dedicated chaperones.18,19 [...] The T6SS apparatus is composed of three core components: the baseplate complex (TssE, TssF, TssG, TssK, VgrG, PAAR), tube-sheath complex (Hcp, TssB, TssC), and membrane complex(TssJ, TssL, TssM). In addition, ClpV, an ATPase for releasing and recycling sheath subunits from contracted sheath, and an additional set of regulatory and accessory proteins for specialized functions are indispensable.14,15 In T6SS assembly, the Hcp tube polymerizes, surrounded by a sheath (TssB and TssC) that also [...] The β helix pattern in the spike region of _B.fragilis_ VgrG differs from the regular hydrophobic-hydrophilic-hydrophobic repeat pattern in _P.aeruginosa_,28 mainly consisting of continuously hydrophobic residues and forming a largely hydrophobic environment in the interior (Figures 6E, S7E, and S7F). VgrG spike in _B.fragilis_ reveals a long β spiral-helix sandwiched between two β meanders, without an extended domain or additional effector domain at its C terminus (Figure S9D). [...] Image 17
