Content: Calcium is one of the most important and common minerals in your body. PTH also helps control the levels of phosphorus (a mineral) and vitamin D (a hormone) in your blood and bones.

Your hormones are chemical messengers that work hard behind the scenes to keep you healthy. And parathyroid hormone is no different. It keeps your blood calcium levels in check so your nerves, muscles and heart can function properly.

### What is the function of parathyroid hormone? [...] Locations:

