Content: Home About cancer Brain tumours Treatment for brain tumours Radiotherapy for brain tumours Side effects of radiotherapy for brain tumours # Side effects of radiotherapy for brain tumours Radiotherapy to the brain can cause short term side effects such as tiredness and sickness. Radiotherapy to the brain can cause hair loss or thinning. Whereas treatment to try to cure your cancer uses a high dose of radiation and so permanent hair loss is much more common. Radiotherapy for brain tumours can sometimes make symptoms worse before they get better. So the treatment tends to have fewer or milder side effects, than regular radiotherapy to the brain. * ## Having radiotherapy for brain tumours
