Title: A20 Xenograft Model
URL: https://www.xenograft.net/a20-xenograft-model/
Content: In today’s therapeutic development pipeline, the mouse xenograft model remains a crucial preclinical system for exploring novel therapeutics. The A20 CDX model (cell line derived xenograft) is an allograft model that benefits from the host mouse containing a fully competent immune system. This model is employed in tumor growth inhibition _in vivo_ studies utilizing these combinations: 1) The fusion protein L19-IL2 co-administered with rituximab to induce complete tumor remission, and 2) [...] The A20 cell line has several characteristics that make it a useful tool for cancer research. It is able to grow in culture and is tumorigenic when injected into mice. It is also known to be highly sensitive to apoptosis, making it useful for studying the mechanisms of cell death and survival in cancer cells. [...] Close

