Content: Alpha thalassemia: MedlinePlus Genetics URL of this page: https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/condition/alpha-thalassemia/ Image 6: Email this page to a friend%3A%20Trusted%20Health%20Information%20for%20you%0A%0ATo%20get%20updates%20by%20email%20when%20new%20information%20becomes%20available%20on%20MedlinePlus%2C%20sign%20up%20at%20https%3A%2F%2Fmedlineplus.gov%2Flistserv.html. Two types of alpha thalassemia can cause health problems. The substitution of Hb Bart or HbH for normal hemoglobin causes anemiaImage 14 and the other serious health problems associated with alpha thalassemia. Nondeletion variants in one or two alleles cause a range of conditions, from alpha thalassemia silent carrier to HbH disease, depending on the allele involved. If both parents are missing at least one alpha-globin allele, their children are at risk of having Hb Bart syndrome, HbH disease, or alpha thalassemia trait. *   Genetic Testing Registry: alpha ThalassemiaImage 15: From the National Institutes of Health
