Title: Alpha Thalassemia | Johns Hopkins Medicine
URL: https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/conditions-and-diseases/alpha-thalassemia
Content: # Alpha Thalassemia ## What is alpha thalassemia? There are 2 main types of thalassemia: alpha and beta. There are 4 types of alpha thalassemia: ## What are the symptoms of alpha thalassemia? Different people will have different symptoms based on which type of alpha thalassemia is inherited. * **Alpha thalassemia silent carrier.** This type has no symptoms. * **Alpha thalassemia carrier.** You may have mild anemia. You have a greater risk of having a child with the most severe type, alpha thalassemia major. People with alpha thalassemia may have no symptoms. * There are 4 different types of alpha thalassemia. * This condition causes mild to severe anemia, based on the type of alpha thalassemia that is inherited.
