Title: Alpha Thalassemia Trait - Together by St. Jude™
URL: https://together.stjude.org/en-us/medical-care/inherited-risk-genetic-testing/alpha-thalassemia-trait.html
Content: Alpha thalassemia trait is a change (mutation) in a gene that helps make hemoglobin in red blood cells. Their children might be at risk for more severe alpha thalassemia including **hemoglobin H** disease or **hydrops fetalis**. If you have alpha thalassemia trait, you do not have hemoglobin H disease and cannot develop it later in life. *   If one parent has the _cis_ form of alpha thalassemia trait (αα/--), and the other parent is a silent carrier (αα/α-), there is a 1 in 4 (25%) chance with each pregnancy of having a child with hemoglobin H disease. Early medical care for alpha thalassemia is important to prevent and manage health problems. *   Early medical care for alpha thalassemia is important to prevent and manage health problems.
