Title: Overview: Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease
URL: https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/creutzfeldt-jakob-disease-cjd/
Content: **Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (CJD) is a rare and fatal condition that affects the brain. ## Symptoms of CJD ## What causes CJD? The precise cause of sporadic CJD is unclear, but it's been suggested that a normal brain protein changes abnormally (""misfolds"") and turns into a prion. The prion that causes variant CJD can also be transmitted by blood transfusion, although this has only happened 5 times in the UK. Familial CJD is a very rare genetic condition where one of the genes a person inherits from their parent (the prion protein gene) carries a mutation that causes prions to form in their brain during adulthood, triggering the symptoms of CJD. In 2020, there were 6 deaths from familial CJD and similar inherited prion diseases in the UK.
