Title: Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease - Causes
URL: https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/creutzfeldt-jakob-disease-cjd/causes/
Content: **Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease (CJD) is caused by an abnormal infectious protein in the brain called a prion.** ## How prions cause CJD The different types of CJD are all caused by a build-up of prions in the brain. Sporadic CJD is more likely to occur in people who have specific versions of the prion protein gene. There's clear evidence that variant CJD (vCJD) is caused by the same strain of prions that causes bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE, or ""mad cow"" disease). Familial or inherited CJD is a rare form of CJD caused by an inherited mutation (abnormality) in the gene that produces the prion protein. The altered gene seems to produce misfolded prions that cause CJD.
