Content: Background: High ALDH1 expression correlates with more aggressive breast cancer subtypes. The works of several authors have proven that a higher ALDH1 expression corresponds to chemotherapy resistance and lower survival rate. Ginestier et al. have demonstrated that ALDH1 (aldehyde dehydrogenase type I) can be a better marker for the breast cancer stem cells profile, the high quantity of which in the tumor is a bad prognosis predictor. Methods: In the present research we have analyzed the ALDH1 [...] obtained through detailed studies of medical documentation and through dynamic monitoring of the patients. Results: The analysis of dependence of time period till the development of metastases on the ALDH1 expression has statistically proved the decrease of time period till the advance of the disease at high expression (ALDH1(high)) with BC patients as compared to the patients with low expression (ALDH1(low)). Similar regularity has been observed during studies of general survival rate. The [...] Home /
