# Benefits of Open Access

## Benefits to authors

A key benefit of open access for authors is that it may increase the reach of your research.

Various studies show an OA citation advantage, e.g.

> ""Of a sample of 4633 articles examined, 2280 (49%) were OA and had a mean citation count of 9.04, whereas the mean for TA articles was 5.76."" (Norris, 2008) [...] ### Other benefits

Among many other benefits cited for OA publication are: [...] access restriction clearly increases the likelihood that the article will be read.
