s. Hoechst [...] SDF1α (CXCL12) is a well-characterized chemokine that plays a critical role in metastasis and invasion in melanoma as well as lung and breast cancer (53–56). SDF1α signals through the CXCR4, a G protein-coupled receptor, to activate signaling pathways required for cell proliferation, survival and migration. Interestingly, Src kinase is required for SDF1α-induced survival of metastatic breast cancer cells (37). Thus, we examined whether Abl kinases were activated in response to SDF1α in
