Title: Congruent Visual Speech Enhances Cortical Entrainment ... - PubMed
URL: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26490860/
Content: Congruent audiovisual speech enhances our ability to comprehend a speaker, even in noise-free conditions. When incongruent auditory and visual information is presented concurrently, it can hinder a listener's perception and even cause him or her to perceive information that was not presented in either modality. Efforts to investigate the neural basis of these effects have often focused on the special case of discrete audiovisual syllables that are spatially and temporally congruent, with less [...] ### Page navigation

