n of inflammatory cells in the lung in diseases such as asthma. In this report, the authors show that the chemokine receptor CX3CR1 is critical to the development of airway inflammation in a mouse model of asthma. CXC3CR1-deficient mice and mice receiving CXC3CR1-blocking reagents had significantly impaired airway hyperresponsiveness, cellular infiltrate and Th2 cytokine production. Adoptive transfer of
