Content: **Keywords:** Innate lymphoid cells (ILCs), gut microbiota, inflammatory bowel disease (IBD), mucosal immunity One of the first studies describes that in a _Helicobacter hepaticus_-induced IBD model, an increase in colonic IL-17- and IFNγ-producing RORγt+ CD127+ NCR− ILC3s drives intestinal inflammation and depletion of these cells leads to abrogation of disease (30). Similarly, flagellin activation of TLR5 in LP mononuclear phagocytes leads to IL-23 production and augments IL-22 by RORγt+ ILCs. Increased IL-22 can lead to subsequent expression of antimicrobial peptides, such as Reg3g, by intestinal epithelial cells (IECs) (39–41), thus promoting gut mucosal protection. [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar%20immune%20precursors%20reside%20in%20human%20adult%20intestine%20and%20differentiate%20into%20natural%20killer%20cells&author=H%20Chinen&author=K%20Matsuoka&author=T%20Sato&author=N%20Kamada&author=S%20Okamoto&volume=133&issue=2&publication_year=2007&pages=559-573&pmid=17681176&doi=10.1053/j.gastro.2007.05.017&)] [DOI] [PubMed] [Google ScholarNKp46(%E2%88%92)%20and%20NKp44(%E2%88%92)NKp46(+)%20natural%20killer%20cells%20in%20the%20intestinal%20mucosa%20of%20patients%20with%20Crohn%27s%20disease&author=T%20Takayama&author=N%20Kamada&author=H%20Chinen&author=S%20Okamoto&author=MT%20Kitazume&volume=139&issue=3&publication_year=2010&pages=882-892&pmid=20638936&doi=10.1053/j.gastro.2010.05.040&)] [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar%20lymphoid%20tissue-inducer%20cells%20promote%20innate%20immunity%20in%20the%20gut&author=GF%20Sonnenberg&author=LA%20Monticelli&author=MM%20Elloso&author=LA%20Fouser&author=D%20Artis&volume=34&issue=1&publication_year=2011&pages=122-134&pmid=21194981&doi=10.1016/j.immuni.2010.12.009&)] [DOI] [PubMed] [Google Scholar%20LTi-like%20innate%20lymphoid%20cells%20by%20Toll-like%20receptor%202&author=NK%20Crellin&author=S%20Trifari&author=CD%20Kaplan&author=N%20Satoh-Takayama&author=JP%20Di%20Santo&volume=33&issue=5&publication_ye