Title: The dual missions of FoxO3a in inflammatory diseases: Regulation ...
URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1567576925003595
Content: In general, FoxO3a regulates its activity through various post-translational modifications and plays a crucial role in inflammatory diseases. It can alleviate oxidative stress by regulating the expression of antioxidant enzymes. In addition, FoxO3a is also involved in multiple programmed cell death processes, including autophagy, apoptosis, and pyroptosis, and these processes are crucial for maintaining the balance between cell survival and death. In various inflammatory diseases, changes in [...] Inflammatory diseases are generally accompanied by the over - production of reactive oxygen species (ROS). These ROS can damage cellular structures, modify cellular functions, and activate inflammatory signaling pathways, thus triggering or exacerbating the inflammatory response. The cellular antioxidant enzyme system, exemplified by a variety of enzymes, catalyzes the reactions that convert ROS into harmless metabolites . Additionally, antioxidant enzymes influence the inflammatory process by [...] ROS plays a crucial role in the cellular signaling and pathophysiology of inflammatory diseases . ROS can directly damage biological macromolecules such as proteins, lipids, and nucleic acids, ultimately leading to cellular death. In addition, ROS is directly involved in the exacerbation of inflammation through various pathways . In inflamed tissues or organisms, a delicate balance between the generation and clearance of ROS is maintained by the antioxidant enzyme system and various PCD [...] The forkhead box protein O3a (FoxO3a) transcription factor is widely involved in the occurrence and development of numerous inflammatory diseases, including sepsis caused by infections and autoimmune diseases such as systemic lupus erythematosus and rheumatoid arthritis. Under various stress conditions, the FoxO3a transcription factor is activated and initiates a series of transcriptional programs to counteract these stresses and restore homeostasis. When homeostasis cannot be restored, FoxO3a [...] variable environments. Consequently, FoxO3a is emerging as a key mediator in the regulation of these processes and represents an important target for future therapeutic development of related diseases.
