Title: T cells in health and disease | Signal Transduction and Targeted ...
URL: https://www.nature.com/articles/s41392-023-01471-y
Content: In this review, we comprehensively summarize the current understandings of T cell biology and functions in both physiological and pathological settings, including the following points: (1) describe the T cell development regarding their differentiation process, T cell lineage commitment, β-selection, and CD4/CD8 lineage choice; (2) introduce major CD4+ and CD8+ T cell classification, differentiation, and the underlying regulatory mechanisms; (3) further discuss how CD8+ and CD4+ T cells respond, differentiate and contribute in infectious diseases, chronic infections and tumors, and autoimmune diseases; (4) γδ T cell development, effector subsets and function in tissue surveillance, infection, and tumor immunity; (5) T cell-based immunotherapies in cancer and autoimmune diseases and their clinical applications. *Cell* **185**, 4471–4473 (2022).
