Content: Structural basis for Parkinson’s disease-linked LRRK2’s binding to microtubules | Nature Structural & Molecular Biology We report a cryo-EM structure of the catalytic half of LRRK2, containing its kinase, in a closed conformation, and GTPase domains, bound to microtubules. A 14-Å structure of LRRK2 carrying the p.I2020T PD mutation bound to microtubules in cells was obtained using cryo-electron tomography (cryo-ET)34.""). In the models, the ROC GTPase domain faces the microtubule, although the cryo-ET structure did not reveal any direct interactions between LRRK2 and the microtubule34.""). **g**, The LRRK2 RCKW domains (ROC, COR-A, COR-B, kinase N-lobe, kinase C-lobe, WD40) (PDB:6VNO) were fitted individually into the 4.5-Å cryo-EM map.
