r types. [...] Current chemotherapeutic agents, in sufficient concentrations, are potent enough to kill cancer cells. Nonetheless, failure of standard chemotherapies for the treatment of desmoplastic cancers (e.g. breast and pancreatic cancers) is in large part due to the fact that these drugs are unable to reach cancer cells in amounts sufficient to cause complete cure . In these tumors, blood vessels are compressed and sometimes collapsed, drastically reducing perfusion and resulting in insufficient
