Content: Red Cross RBC products utilize leukoreduction, which reduces the incidence of alloimmunization to foreign human leukocyte antigens (HLA) and febrile nonhemolytic transfusion reactions. Studies indicate that prestorage leukoreduction of RBCs is as effective in preventing transfusion-transmitted cytomegalovirus (CMV) as use of CMV seronegative (CMV antibody-negative) components.

Indications: [...] CMV is an intracellular virus transmissible by cellular blood components which may have a detrimental effect on immunocompromised patients. Universal leukoreduction of red blood cell products has decreased the risk of transfusion-transmitted CMV infection. However, upon request, CMV-negative products can be provided.

Indications:

## Specialized Blood Products & Services [...] ## Red Blood Cell Products

Red blood cells (RBCs) are given to patients with bleeding, anemia, or other hematologic conditions. The Red Cross offers a full complement of RBCs to meet both adult and pediatric/neonatal transfusion needs. All products are leukoreduced and available for all ABO/RhD blood types. [...] Red blood cells are sometimes washed to remove excess potassium, cytokines, antibodies and plasma proteins that might cause an adverse transfusion reaction. The Red Cross can additionally provide high hematocrit washed RBCs with the unit tagged with the measured hematocrit. These products have an expiration time of 24 hours from the wash time.

## Product Description [...] Red blood cells from donors with rare blood types can be frozen in glycerol solutions and then stored for 10 years or more. Once thawed, the glycerol must be removed prior to transfusion. RBCs recovered in this manner have the same clinical efficacy as refrigerated products.
