Title: The use of leukoreduced red blood cell products is associated with ...
URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0002961008002353
Content: This retrospective before-and-after study demonstrated that the use of leukoreduced RBC transfusion products in injured patients results in decreased rates of pneumonia and overall infectious complications. We found that use of leukoreduced RBC products after injury was associated with a significant reduction in risk of pneumonia and the development of any type of infectious complication. Within the subset of patients receiving massive transfusions, the use of leukoreduced RBC products after [...] ### Conclusion

Prestorage leukoreduction is associated with a reduction of infectious complications in injured patients. Furthermore, this protective effect appears more pronounced in patients receiving massive transfusion (>6 U packed RBCs).

