Content: While our findings indicate that macrolides could potentially offer cardiovascular protection, it is worth noting that some other studies have not yielded similar results. The Azithromycin in Acute Coronary Syndrome (AZACS) study , the Weekly Intervention with Zithromax for Atherosclerosis and its Related Disorders (WIZARD) study  and the Azithromycin and Coronary Events Study (ACES)  reported that azithromycin provided a neutral effect in the secondary prevention of atherosclerosis [...] antimicrobial effects . Although the broader anti-inflammatory properties of MMT suggest potential cardioprotective effects, historical studies reported an increased incidence of sudden cardiac death or ventricular tachyarrhythmias associated with the use of short-term courses of macrolides [8–10]. The impact of MMT on cardiovascular outcomes in individuals with bronchiectasis has not been extensively studied and thus the balance of risk or potential benefits is unclear. [...] The primary outcome of interest was three-point major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE), a composite of cardiovascular death, acute myocardial infarction (AMI) and stroke. Secondary outcomes included each component of MACE and all-cause mortality. The safety outcome was a composite of ventricular arrhythmias and sudden cardiac death. We chose hip fracture hospitalisation as negative control outcome in the comparison analysis. Each individual was followed up for a fixed duration of 5 years. [...] Overview of the study. MMT: macrolide maintenance therapy; ICD-9: International Classification of Diseases, Ninth Revision; PSM: propensity score matching; MACE: major adverse cardiovascular events; AMI: acute myocardial infarction.

