Title: Lysine Acetylation and Its Role in Protein Regulation - Nature
URL: https://www.nature.com/research-intelligence/nri-topic-summaries/lysine-acetylation-and-its-role-in-protein-regulation-micro-63068
Content: Lysine acetylation is a reversible post-translational modification that plays a critical role in modulating protein function, stability and interactions across a range of organisms. This modification, which involves the covalent attachment of an acetyl group to the ε-amino group of lysine residues, is increasingly recognised as a pivotal regulator of cellular metabolism, gene expression and even pathogenicity. By altering the charge and conformation of target proteins, lysine acetylation can [...] ## Technical Terms

Lysine Acetylation: A reversible chemical modification involving the attachment of an acetyl group to the lysine residue of a protein, affecting its function and interaction capacity.

Acetyltransferase: An enzyme that catalyses the transfer of an acetyl group from an acetyl donor, such as acetyl-CoA, to lysine residues on target proteins.

Deacetylase: An enzyme responsible for removing acetyl groups from lysine residues, thereby reversing the effects of acetylation. [...] Recent studies have advanced our understanding of the mechanistic aspects of lysine acetylation. One investigation elucidated how acetylation regulates acetyl-CoA synthetase activity via conformational changes in the enzyme complex, providing novel insights into the interplay between metabolic substrates and enzymatic regulation . Complementary to this, a comprehensive review of protein post-translational modifications in bacteria has highlighted the widespread occurrence and diverse functions [...] Independent studies have further highlighted the importance of lysine acetylation across diverse biological systems. A recent proteomic analysis has detailed the acetylation landscape of ribosomal proteins, linking acetylation homeostasis to the efficient assembly and function of the ribosome, with implications for translational fidelity and antibiotic sensitivity . Moreover, investigations into bacterial pathogens have shown that deacetylation processes modulated by enzymes such as CobB can [...] of lysine acetylation, revealing its influence on cellular processes from protein synthesis to stress response . In addition, research focused on plant systems has demonstrated that lysine acetylation not only modulates key metabolic enzymes but also plays an integral role in photosynthetic regulation, thereby underscoring the modification’s broad biological significance . Together, these findings underscore the global impact of lysine acetylation on protein regulation and suggest new avenues
