lation of histones was subsequently discovered in the early 1970s24.""),25.""). Similar to other PTMs, two groups of writer and eraser enzymes, methyltransferases and demethylases, dynamically regulate the methylation state of target proteins26.""). Lysine residues offer three possible forms of methylation—mono-methyl, di-methyl, and tri-methyl–while for arginine residues,
