With the exception of bolus regimens, which are no longer preferred, there is relative equivalence in efficacy among fluoropyrimidine-based regimens. Capecitabine can be safely combined with oxaliplatin, yielding similar outcomes compared with FOLFOX; however, when capecitabine is combined with irinotecan, the results are less consistent. In the absence of more data, CAPIRI would not be recommended as an alternative to FOLFIRI because of toxicity.
