Content: The intrinsic pathway is also called the mitochondrial pathway owing to the essential involvement of mitochondria (Figure 1), which is not only the site where antiapoptotic and proapoptotic proteins interact and determine cell fates, but also the origin of signals that initiate the activation of caspases through various mechanisms. Therefore, here we mainly focus on the mitochondrial proteins that are released during apoptosis and whether or not mitochondria play similar essential roles in invertebrate cell death. Only one year later, back-to-back papers demonstrated that the release of Cyt c from mitochondria is a primary site for Bcl-2 regulation of apoptosis (69, 146), firmly establishing an active role of mitochondria in apoptosis. [DOI] [PMC free article] [PubMed] [Google Scholar%20irreversibly%20inactivates%20IAPs%20and%20facilitates%20caspase%20activity%20in%20apoptosis&author=QH%20Yang&author=R%20Church-Hajduk&author=J%20Ren&author=ML%20Newton&author=C%20Du&volume=17&publication_year=2003&pages=1487-1496&pmid=12815069&doi=10.1101/gad.1097903&)]
