ymidine analogue mutations (TAMs) M41L and T215Y/F (_p_< 0.001), the lamivudine resistance mutations M184V/I (_p_< 0.001), and non-nucleoside RTI (NNRTI) resistance mutations K103N and Y181C/I (_p_< 0.001). The association with TAMs and NNRTI resistance mutations was consistent with the selection of N348I in patients treated with regimens that included both zidovudine and nevirapine (odds ratio 2.62, 95% confidence interval 1.43–4.81). The appearance of N348I was
