mbrane, [...] Increased intracellular calcium concentration during oxidative stress activates calcineurin, which dephosphorylates and activates NFAT transcription factors 1–4. The activated NFAT transcription factors enter the nucleus, bind to DNA enhancer or promoter regions, and regulate the transcription of downstream genes. Different downstream target genes of NFAT lead to different effects. NFAT, acting on NOX, can affect ROS levels, regulate potassium channels to affect mitochondrial membrane potential
