Content: _NR5A2_ is an important orphan nuclear receptor within the NR5A family . This gene is highly conserved across species and typically regulates gene expression by interacting with DNA response elements . In vertebrates, the NR5A family is divided into two subfamilies: _NR5A1_, also known as steroidogenic factor 1 (_SF-1_), which is predominantly expressed in steroidogenic tissues, and _NR5A2_, also known as liver receptor homolog-1 (_LRH-1_), which is mainly expressed in endoderm-derived tissues [...] In the present study, the regulatory effects of _NR5A2_ knockdown on gonad development and the underlying mechanisms were investigated in detail in _C. farreri_. RNA-seq, WGCNA, and GSEA revealed that _NR5A2_ knockdown significantly reduced the expression of genes involved in sex differentiation and affected steroidogenesis and cholesterol metabolism, thereby hindering normal gonadal development. The findings provide a new perspective to elucidate the molecular mechanism of gonadal development [...] comprehensive investigation that combined RNA-seq, weighted gene co-expression network analysis (WGCNA), gene set enrichment analysis (GSEA), and histological analysis. This approach enabled a detailed exploration of the regulatory mechanisms of _NR5A2_ in reproductive development, providing valuable insights into the reproductive endocrinology of bivalves. [...] Steroid hormones play a crucial role in regulating reproductive development in vertebrates. Adrenal steroids are essential for glucose metabolism and stress response, whereas gonadal steroids are key to sex differentiation and reproductive development , . The synthesis of steroid hormones begins with cholesterol as a precursor, catalyzed by enzymes such as P450 side chain cleavage enzymes and hydroxysteroid dehydrogenases . In this process, nuclear receptor subfamily 5 group A member 2 [...] 2025, Comparative Biochemistry and Physiology Part B Biochemistry and Molecular Biology  Show abstract The scallop (_C