Content: recently emerged (Botrugno et al., 2004). Therefore, NR5A2 clearly appears to be a crucial factor that promotes proper development and function of the enterohepatic system (Botrugno et al., 2004; Paré et al., 2004). In the adult, _NR5A2_ is not only expressed in tissues of endodermal origins but also in steroidogenic tissues, such as pre-adipocytes (Clyne et al., 2002), the ovary (Boerboom et al., 2000; Schoonjans et al., 2002; Sirianni et al., 2002; Falender et al., 2003; Hinshelwood et al., [...] Because _NR5A2_ is expressed in the VE before gastrulation, it raises the possibility that the phenotype observed in _NR5A2_−/− embryos might result from defects in the formation and/or function of this tissue. To test this possibility, the expression of two VE marker genes, _HNF4_ and _GATA4_, which have been shown to be important for the formation and/or function of this tissue, was examined by whole-mount in situ hybridization (Chen et al., 1994; Duncan et al., 1994, 1997; Soudais et al., [...] Recently, _NR5A2_ was shown to be expressed early during mouse embryogenesis (Paré et al., 2004; Gu et al., 2005). Indeed, _NR5A2_ is ubiquitously expressed during preimplantation stages of development. Shortly after implantation, _NR5A2_ transcripts are detected in the visceral endoderm (VE), an extraembryonic tissue of crucial importance for proper growth and patterning of the embryo (Bielinska et al., 1999; Paré et al., 2004). Consistent with the early expression pattern of _NR5A2_, a [...] _HNF1α_ (Rausa et al., 1999; Paré et al., 2001). In turn, the expression of _NR5A2_ is controlled by early endodermal transcription factors, including GATA4, GATA6, and HNF4, as well as by other developmental transcription factors from the nuclear receptor, basic helix–loop–helix, and homeodomain families (Paré et al., 2001; Annicotte et al., 2003). NR5A2, therefore, acts downstream of transcription factors important for endoderm specification and upstream of genes involved in hepatopancreatic [...] Previous studies based on the expression pattern of _NR5A2_ and on both electrophoretic mobility shift and transient transfection assays have implicated NR5A2 as a key factor involved in the transcriptional cascade leading to endoderm specification and liver determination. During early embryogenesis, the VE displays a gene expression profile that recapitulates the endodermal program of gene expression and fulfills endodermal functions (Bielinska et al., 1999). As a number of liver-specific
Score: 0.76888984


