Content: Inspired by our previous success in the synthesis of aptamer-conjugated liposomes for targeted cancer cell drug delivery (Baek et al., 2014, Kim et al., 2019, Kim et al., 2018, Kim et al., 2022), we designed LNPs armored with DNA aptamers for specific PTEN mRNA delivery (Apt-LNP[PTEN mRNA]) to prostate cancer cells (Scheme 1). To achieve the targeted delivery of LNP harboring PTEN mRNA, we conjugated anti-PD-L1 DNA aptamers, which exclusively bind to the PD-L1 cell surface marker overexpressed [...] oligonucleotides with structural conformations that provide a robust capacity for the recognition of cell surface molecules and that can be used for directed targeting. Aptamers can be directly conjugated to therapeutic RNA molecules, in the form of aptamer-oligonucleotide chimeras, or incorporated into nanoparticles used as vehicles for the delivery of these therapeutics. Herein, we discuss the use of aptamers for cell-directed RNA therapies, provide an overview of different types of [...] •Conjugation of cancer cell-targeting PD-L1 DNA aptamer to LNPs forms Apt-LNP. 
   •Apt-LNP achieves specific delivery of PTEN mRNA to prostate cancer cells. 
   •Delivered PTEN mRNA induces apoptotic cell death in prostate cancer cells. 
   •Targeted PTEN mRNA delivery with Apt-LNP reduces tumor growth _in vivo_. 

