e, advanced mouse models such as C3HeB/FeJ9."") or interleukin (IL)-13-overexpressing (tg)10."") mice, which reflect the pathology of human TB in many aspects, are increasingly used for an improved pre-clinical evaluation of new drugs by assessing their potential to penetrate centrally necrotizing granulomas and thus predict their local antimycobacterial activity11.""),12.""),13."").
