Pseudogene PTENP1 regulates the expression of PTEN by functioning as an miRNA decoy.,1,"Title: PTENP1 - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics
URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/agricultural-and-biological-sciences/ptenp1
Content: The PTEN pseudogene PTENP1 was the first pseudogene to be characterized as a ceRNA. It has been shown to regulate PTEN expression by sponging PTEN-targeting miRNAs (miR-17, miR-19, miR-21, miR-26, and miR-214 families) . This in turn led to a reduction in growth and invasiveness of many cancers, such as prostate cancer, melanoma, endometrial cancer (EC), clear-cell renal cell carcinoma (ccRCC), hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC), and gastric cancer . Another well-studied oncosuppressive pseudogene [...] initiator methionine codon, it still possesses a 3′ UTR with high homology to PTEN. As a result, increased expression of PTENP1 serves as a “decoy” for PTEN targeting miRNA and leads to increased translation and protein levels of biologically functional PTEN. Therefore, pseudogenes are now going to have to be considered when analyzing various functions of miRNA. [...] Downregulation of the tumor suppressor, _PTEN_, has been associated with numerous types of cancers (Cairns et al., 1997; Li et al., 1997; Vlietstra, van Alewijk, Hermans, van Steenbrugge, & Trapman, 1998). The lncRNA, _PTENpg1_ (also known as _PTENP1)_, is selectively lost in cancer, has similar expression levels to that of _PTEN_, and functions as an miRNA decoy by intercepting miRNA species targeting _PTEN_ (Poliseno et al., 2010). Two _PTENpg1_ antisense (as) isoforms, _α_ and _β_, regulate [...] During the course of assembling references for this chapter, the expanding complexity of miRNA and more specifically, metastamiR, exploded. As targets are assigned to individual miRNA, one must now take into account previously ignored pseudogenes. Poliseno et al. showed that the pseudogene, PTENP1, was biologically active by virtue of regulating cellular levels of the tumor suppressor PTEN (Poliseno et al., 2010). Although PTENP1 is not translated into protein due to a missense mutation of the [...] lncRNA PTENP1-encoded antisense RNA (PTENP1-AsRNA) was identified as a regulator of _PTEN_ transcription and PTEN RNA stability. There are two isoforms, α and β. The α-isoform is found on the _PTEN_ promoter, where it recruits _DNMT3_ and _EZH2_ to modulate PTEN transcription epigenetically. The β-isoform interacts with PTENP1, affecting PTEN protein expression, by changing the stability of PTENP1 and miRNA sponge activity . Expression of PTEN is regulated by many ncRNAs at many levels,
