Content: Summary Recent studies have revealed that transcripts associated with the PTEN pseudogene can markedly influence cellular behavior through microRNA‐mediated regulatory loops. In a spinal cord injury model, interference with PTENP1 expression (using PTENP1-shRNA) was shown to disrupt the balance of key microRNAs—namely, miR-21 and miR-19b—thereby indirectly modulating PTEN expression and subsequently increasing neuronal apoptosis. These findings underscore how modulation of PTEN pseudogene [...] HGNC FamilyNon-coding RNAs
Name PTENP1 antisense RNA
Description PTENP1-AS encodes an antisense RNA (asRNA) of PTENP1, a PTEN (phosphatase and tensin homolog) pseudogene. PTENP1 regulates PTEN by both sense (GeneID: 11191) and antisense RNAs. This antisense RNA (PTENP1-AS) regulates PTEN transcription and mRNA stability. [provided by RefSeq, Jun 2020] [...] In the context of malignant melanoma, the PTEN pseudogene antisense RNA (PTENP1-AS) has been identified as a negative regulator of PTEN transcription. Here, increased PTENP1-AS expression in BRAFi-resistant melanoma cells promotes the recruitment of epigenetic modifiers such as EZH2 and enhances H3K27me3 methylation at the PTEN promoter, leading to its downregulation. This epigenetic silencing contributes not only to drug resistance against BRAF inhibitors but also correlates with poorer [...] Zhan Wang, Yuxin Song, Xingwen Han, et al. Long noncoding RNA PTENP1 affects the recovery of spinal cord injury by regulating the expression of miR-19b and miR-21._J Cell Physiol (2020)_ DOI: 10.1002/jcp.29253 PMID: 31583718

