Content: West Nile virus (WNV) is a member of Japanese encephalitis serogroup of _Flavivirus_ genus, family _Flaviviridae,_ which is distributed globally across temperate and tropical climates . This is a small enveloped virus with ssRNA genome of positive polarity, which is capped, but not polyadenylated . Viral genomic RNA encodes for 3 structural, 7 non-structural proteins and viral noncoding RNA (reviewed in [2,3:13–25.""),4]). WNV circulates between _Culex Sp._ mosquitos and birds but can also be [...] RNASeq analysis revealed that WNV infection and IFN-alpha treatment also alter secretion of mRNAs in EVs. In EVs from WNV infected cells, 1182 mRNAs had increased level compared to mock and levels of 161 mRNAs were decreased (Fig. 4a, Additional file 4: Table S5). In EVs secreted by IFN-treated cells, 1356 increased and 72 decreased mRNAs were identified (Fig. 4b. Additional file 4: Table S6).

