URL: https://ashpublications.org/blood/article/115/16/3196/27031/Ribosomopathies-human-disorders-of-ribosome
Content: Ribosomopathies compose a collection of disorders in which genetic abnormalities cause impaired ribosome biogenesis and function, resulting in specific clinical phenotypes. Congenital mutations in _RPS19_ and other genes encoding ribosomal proteins cause Diamond-Blackfan anemia, a disorder characterized by hypoplastic, macrocytic anemia. Mutations in other genes required for normal ribosome biogenesis have been implicated in other rare congenital syndromes, Schwachman-Diamond syndrome, [...] DBA was originally described by Josephs in a review of anemia in infancy and childhood in 193612 and later categorized by Diamond and Blackfan as a congenital hypoplastic anemia.12,13 The disorder is characterized by anemia, macrocytosis, reticulocytopenia, and a selective decrease or absence of erythroid precursors in an otherwise normocellular bone marrow.9 The incidence is estimated to be 4 to 5 cases per million live births, and there are 595 patients currently registered in the [...] Cartilage hair hypoplasia [...] View largeDownload PPT [...] View largeDownload PPT
