Title: Bcl-2 dependent modulation of Hippo pathway in cancer cells
URL: https://biosignaling.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s12964-024-01647-1
Content: Bcl-2 or Bcl-xL in human melanoma cells. Among the peculiar Bcl-2 modulated pathways, we focused on Hippo Pathway, a highly conserved signalling pathway among organisms. Studies of Hippo pathway in human tumors clarified that its deregulation leads to YAP/TAZ activation, which in turn promotes the development and progression of different types of cancer \\[20\\]. This pathway consists of a kinase cascade that begins with MST1/2 which phosphorylates LATS1/2, large protein kinases with tumor [...] degree of stiffness, such as 1 kPa resembling normal tissue, or 50 kPa, representing a slightly stiffer environment similar to what is found in tumours \\[36:3166–82."")\\]. According to published data \\[36:3166–82."")\\], A375 cells plated on 50 kPa gel showed increased viability than cells seeded in lower stiff conditions, 1 kPa, due to their nature of aggressive solid tumor cells (Fig. 7A, B). Interestingly, Bcl-2 silencing abrogated the ability of A375 cells to growth in 50 kPa stiffness [...] models we previously demonstrated Bcl-2 modulation of tumor progression-associated properties and tumor metastatization \\[10:414–21.""),11:1024–35.""),12:2558–67."")\\]. In melanoma cells, we also described the Bcl-2-mediated regulation of microRNA-211 and mitochondrial transcript levels through the interaction with SLIRP \\[13:2304–12.""), 14:e2090."")\\]. Likewise, we described the pivotal role played by Bcl-2 in orchestrating the crosstalk between melanoma cells and tumor microenvironment (TME) [...] components, such as neovascular endothelial cells, through a mechanism involving vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF), and tumor-associated macrophages through interleukin-1β induction of the M2 phenotype \\[11:1024–35.""), 15.""), 16:1453–5."")\\]. Regarding Bcl-xL, we reported its role in the modulation of properties strictly related to melanoma progression and maintenance of cancer stem cell phenotype, \\[17:3216."")\\]. Bcl-xL also regulates in vitro endothelial cell functions and in vivo [...] Moreover, YAP silencing decreased cell viability of Bcl-2 overexpressing clone plated on 50 kPa gel (Fig. 7E, F, Supplementary Fig S6), indicating the involvement of YAP in the ability of Bcl-2 to promote cell viability in higher stiffness condition.
