Content: recruited to damage sites and then activated by Smc5/6. This model postulates that sites requiring Sgs1 function initially recruit Smc5/6. The ATP-dependent remodeling of the complex activates the SUMO E3 ligase to self-SUMOylate Smc5/6 (9, 10). Two SUMO-interacting motifs (SIMs) on Sgs1 then recognize SUMOylated Smc5/6 subunits, thus facilitating their interaction (10, 13). Finally, Smc5/6-dependent SUMOylation of newly recruited Sgs1 and Top3 leads to STR activation (10, 13). Consistent with [...] Smc5/6 hinge has shown an organization reminiscent of the cohesin and condensin hinges but with specialized features. These features include novel hub and latch domains that are important for single-stranded DNA binding and that lead to DNA damage sensitivity following mutation (3). An interesting aspect of the Smc5/6 complex architecture is the presence of a SUMO E3 ligase, Nse2/Mms21 (6, 141), docked to the coiled coil of the Smc5 subunit (33, 113). This provides the complex with the ability [...] not only to SUMOylate a variety of substrates (2, 6, 10, 13, 74, 133, 141) but also to self-SUMOylate (9, 10). Interestingly, the activation of the Nse2/Mms21 ligase function requires binding of ATP to Smc5 at the base of the complex (9), raising the possibility that a conformational change in Smc5 linked to the ATPase cycle is responsible for the activation of Nse2/Mms21-dependent SUMOylation (9). [...] The enzymatic activity of Smc5/6 as an E3 SUMO ligase and its function in recombinational pro-cesses have also been linked to telomere biology. In budding yeast, Smc5/6 mutants show defects in telomere maintenance (141), while in human cells the complex is involved in the alternative length-ening of telomeres (ALT) maintenance pathway (100), a telomerase-independent, HR-dependent pathway that is active in 10–15% of cancers (17). Indeed, cancer cells relying on ALT require Smc5/6 function for HR [...] In plants, the Smc5/6 complex has been most studied in Arabidopsis thaliana , where it has been shown to have specific roles as a developmental regulator. The developmental processes that Smc5/6 impacts include seed and meristem development (49, 54, 140), flowering time (62) and gametophyte development (72). Most studies have focused on the SUMO ligase activity of the complex, analyzing roles of AtNSE2/MMS21 , which is also known as HIGH PLOIDY2 (HPY2 )because the original phenotype increased
