A majority of the sample (N = 15,648 women, N = 13,567 men) was middle-aged (30–59 years) and about half had a primary level of education (Table 1). Nearly all women were non-smokers (96.3%), compared to 32.8% of men. About one-third of women were not working (37.1%), compared to 10.2% of men. Half of the adults resided in urban areas and slightly larger proportions resided in lower (versus higher) wealth households.

