Title: Kidney Paired Donation powerful program reaches milestone
URL: https://www.blood.ca/en/research/our-research-stories/research-education-discovery/kidney-paired-donation-powerful-program
Content: Kidney Paired Donation - how it works

The program is supported by a sophisticated web-based software to optimize the number of donors and transplant candidates matched through the Kidney Paired Donation program.

A matching algorithm is run three times a year to compare the medical information on all the pairs and non-directed donors in the Registry and identifies kidney transplant opportunities. [...] The added benefit to this approach is that patients transplanted through kidney paired donation are not added to the waitlist and this then shortens the waitlist and wait time for those patients who are dependent on receiving a deceased donor transplant. [...] Kidney transplantation is the preferred therapy for patients with kidney failure. Compared with dialysis, transplantation offers significantly longer life expectancy, a better quality of life, considerable cost avoidance per patient to the health care system, and an increased likelihood that the patient will remain employed.

Transplantation of a kidney from a living donor is advantageous to the recipient.The kidney lasts, on average, 25 per cent longer compared to a deceased donor kidney. [...] The Kidney Paired Donation program – launched in 2009 –  is a perfect example of how interprovincial health systems work together to forge success beyond provincial borders and improve access to transplants for patients. [...] The success of this program can be attributed to the selflessness of the more than 500 individuals who have stepped forward to be living organ donors. Kudos to the truly altruistic non-directed anonymous donors (willing, living donors without a specific intended recipient) who make domino kidney exchanges possible.

A recent story on CBC showcases this program and the impact it can have on patients waiting for a transplant and their families.
