lls, such as [...] In normal cells, the YAP/TAZ complex is predominantly found in the cytoplasm, where it can be phosphorylated by LATS1/2 . When the complex is dephosphorylated, usually due to growth factor-related signaling or mechanical stress, it is localized in the nucleus . This nucleocytoplasmic shuttling is regulated by importins, which bind to nuclear localization signals (NLS) on the complex and allow them to be transported into the nucleus through pore complexes . In contrast, exportins bind nuclear
