he entire [...] Fate mapping and gene expression studies show that early heart development is highly conserved in mammalian and avian embryos. In mice, the heart cells are among the first to gastrulate at early to mid-streak stages (Tam et al., 1997). Before gastrulation, mouse epiblast has cardiogenic potential and the cardiac lineage is specified at the late streak stage (Auda-Boucher et al., 2000). The cardiac progenitors migrate from the primitive streak to the most anterior lateral position in the embryo
