Title: Type VI secretion systems of pathogenic and commensal ...
URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2211124722004922
Content: close-contact cells by the T6SS allows for the delivery of a broad arsenal of effectors into the target cell, including antibacterial proteins such as peptidoglycanhydrolases, DNases, phospholipases, and NAD+hydrolases (Diniz et al., 2015; Durand et al., 2014; Hernandez et al., 2020; Jurėnas and Journet, 2021). VgrG and Hcp proteins themselves may act as effectors due to functional C-terminal domains (Brooks et al., 2013; Ma et al., 2009, 2017). T6SS effectors are neutralized by the [...] The T6SS of proteobacterial species is composed of at least 13 core subunits (TssA-TssM), necessary for its assembly and function, which are conserved in both pathogenic and non-pathogenic bacteria (Boyer et al., 2009; Jani and Cotter, 2010). The T6SS uses a spring-like tail to propel a needle loaded with effectors (Santin et al., 2019). The tail is built on an assembly baseplate (TssEFGK) upon which the needle polymerizes. The needle is made of stacked hemolysin-coregulated protein (Hcp) [...] ### T6SS effector protein VgrG1 possesses antibacterial activities against commensal _E.coli_ [...] hexamers, capped by a trimer of the valine-glycine repeat (VgrG) spike protein and is often further sharpened by the PAAR protein (Cascales, 2008; Pukatzki et al., 2007). The inner tube of the tail is wrapped in a contractile sheath, which is composed of two proteins, TssB and TssC. The T6SS tail is docked to the cell envelope by a membrane complex (TssJLM) serving as a channel for passage of the needle upon sheath contraction (Cherrak et al., 2019; Durand et al., 2015). In enteroaggregative [...] nanomachine akin to a molecular crossbow that uses a contractile mechanism to inject effector proteins directly into target cells, where they mediate cytotoxic events. T6SSs are highly versatile, capable of targeting adjacent host cells or bacterial competitors (Basler et al., 2013; Ma and Mekalanos, 2010). Furthermore, although the assembly and multi-protein structure of T6SSs are largely conserved across species of Gram-negative bacteria, their regulation and secreted effector repertoire vary
