Title: Structure and assembly of type VI secretion system cargo delivery ...
URL: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2211124723007921
Content: The T6SS apparatus is composed of three core components: the baseplate complex (TssE, TssF, TssG, TssK, VgrG, PAAR), tube-sheath complex (Hcp, TssB, TssC), and membrane complex(TssJ, TssL, TssM). In addition, ClpV, an ATPase for releasing and recycling sheath subunits from contracted sheath, and an additional set of regulatory and accessory proteins for specialized functions are indispensable.14,15 In T6SS assembly, the Hcp tube polymerizes, surrounded by a sheath (TssB and TssC) that also [...] Bacteria employ various strategies to achieve a competitive advantage against other strains in their environment or in the host.12 Among these strategies, the contact-dependent cell envelope-spanning nanomachine T6SS, which injects species-specific protein effectors into adjacent target cells or the surrounding environment,12,13 plays a crucial role in mediating inter-bacterial species competition in the mammalian intestine. [...] polymerizes around it in a high-energy, extended conformation.16,17 Contraction of the sheath propels the Hcp tube, sharpened by a VgrG-PAAR spike, through the baseplate and into a neighboring cell. Diverse effector proteins are delivered attached to VgrG, PAAR, or loaded into the Hcp tube.13,18 The effector cargo may be attached via specific interactions, which may require dedicated chaperones.18,19 [...] T6SS GA3 is a conserved locus found exclusively in _B.fragilis_, with more than 95% identity between strains within conserved regions.21 The T6SS in _B.fragilis_ NCTC 9343 shares common core components with the representative T6SS-II in _P.aeruginosa_ but differs in orientation and organization (Figure 1A)_._ The effector cargo delivery components VgrG and Hcp from gut symbiotic _B.fragilis_ show distant evolutionary relationships with other well-studied pathogenic members from _Proteobacteria_ [...] _B.fragilis_ NCTC 9343 is a representative strain among _B.fragilis_ with a functional T6SS GA3 locus containing two specific effector-immunity protein pairs that could contribute to inter-species competition.9,10 However, their killing effect seems to only work in some _Bacteroidales_ strains, including ETBF, conferring no advantage when competing with _E.coli_.9 Of note, the core components in the _B.fragilis_ T6SS cargo loading system, Hcp-VgrG-PAAR, exhibit low sequence similarity to other
Score: 0.55912215


