lasmic [...] proteolysis and activation of intermediates in the signalling cascades could participate to hypertrophy and/or the phenotypic shift, like protein kinase C. Here, the main practical implications in doping prevention lie in the two following findings: 1°) high doses of clenbuterol determine a transient deleterious impact on slow twitch muscle, rich in !2-adrenoreceptors, 2°) the ubiquitous calcium dependent proteolysis system is differentially activated in oxidative and glycolytic muscles and
