Title: Chimeric brain models: Unlocking insights into human ...
URL: https://www.cell.com/neuron/fulltext/S0896-6273(25)00256-9
Content: Chimeric brain models: Unlocking insights into human neural development, aging, diseases, and cell therapies: Neuron Chimeric brain models: Unlocking insights into human neural development, aging, diseases, and cell therapies The final insert features an image of a human microglia that has successfully developed and functionally integrated within a chimeric mouse brain, highlighting the highly intricate morphology and complex branching patterns of human microglial cells in the chimeric brain. This figure illustrates the role of human-rodent chimeric brain models in advancing human cell profiling and the development of novel cell therapies for neurological diseases. The _molecular profiling_ section shows how advanced molecular profiling techniques, such as spatial transcriptomics and single-cell multi-omics, enable the identification of human cell-specific features in the chimeric brain, offering insights into the diversity of human neural cells, the underlying mechanisms of neurological diseases, and the restorative properties of cell-replacement therapy strategies.
