Title: Transplanted deep-layer cortical neuroblasts integrate into host ...
URL: https://stemcellres.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s13287-024-04049-9
Content: Human embryonic stem cell (hESCs)-derived cortical neural progenitors have shown great potentials in ischemic stroke in adult brain. By using embryonic body (EB) neural differentiation method combined with DAPT pre-treatment and quantitative cell transplantation, human cortical neuroblasts were obtained and transplanted into the cortex of hypoxic-ischemic injured brain with different dosages 2 weeks after surgery. Transplanted hESCs derived cortical neuroblasts survive, project to endogenous targets, and integrate into host cortical neural circuits to rescue animal behavior in the HIE-injured brain without graft overgrowth, providing a novel and safe cell replacement strategy for the future treatment of HIE. Cortical region-specific engraftment of embryonic stem cell-derived neural progenitor cells restores axonal sprouting to a subcortical target and achieves motor functional recovery in a mouse model of neonatal hypoxic-ischemic brain injury.
