vented growth of [...] reduced TCR diversity was no longer sufficient to ensure rejection of every MC57 variant, as tumors grew in each mouse injected with MC57 or MC57-mp68. However, T cells in 2CxRag+/− animals were able to eliminate transplanted MC57 cells if they expressed the antigen SIY that is recognized by TCR-2C (Table 1). TCR-2C alone was sufficient for this effect because 2CxRag−/− animal also did not develop tumors after transplantation of MC57-SIY cancer cells. Under these conditions, CD4+ T cells were
