Content: Investigators sought to compare the cost-effectiveness of standard treatment (12-week monotherapy) with enhanced varenicline (extended varenicline treatment or nicotine replacement therapy [NRT] in combination with varenicline) use among individuals trying to quit smoking. Point prevalence abstinence of 7 days at 52 weeks (biochemically confirmed) was the primary outcome. [...] The incremental cost-effectiveness ratio (ICER) was $4681 per individual who quit smoking in the 12-week varenicline monotherapy group with $4579 per quality-adjusted life-year (QALY) added. The ICER for 24-week varenicline combination therapy relative to 12-week monotherapy was significantly higher per additional individual who quit smoking. [...] pulmonologyadvisor logo
