# For Smoking Cessation, Varenicline Monotherapy is More Cost Effective Than Enhanced Treatment

Researchers found 12-week varenicline monotherapy for smoking cessation to be most cost effective than enhanced varenicline treatment. These findings were published in the Journal of the American Medical Association Network Open. [...] Total mean (SD) cost strongly favored 12-week monotherapy ($1175 [$365] vs 12-week combination therapy, $1374 [$412]; 24-week monotherapy, $2022 [$813]; 24-week combination therapy, $2118 [$1058]). The 12-week combination therapy cost $199 more on average than 12-week monotherapy but was 0.7% less effective. The 24-week monotherapy cost $847 more on average than 12-week monotherapy but was 1.5% less effective. [...] Among all participants (mean [SD] age, 49.1 [11.9] years; 54.0% women; 69.3% White, 22.9% Black), 881 (70.4%) completed the 52-week follow-up. The investigators found smoking cessation through follow-up was similar between groups (25.1% 12-week monotherapy; 24.4% 24-week monotherapy; 23.6% 12-week combination therapy; 25.1% 24-week combination therapy). Adherence varied by treatment group, highest in 12-week monotherapy (44.1%), lowest in 24-week combination therapy (30.2%).
