dings have indicated that the inhibition of glutamine metabolism can lead to a suppression of cancer cell apoptosis, a process that is believed to be influenced by the level of reactive oxygen species (ROS) metabolism. Zhao et al. found that GLUD1 is highly expressed in hepatocellular carcinoma, which enhances intracellular mitochondrial respiratory activity and generates large amounts of ROS. The excess of ROS leads to increased expression levels of apoptosis-promoting factors p53,
