Title: Glutamine Metabolism in Cancer - NCBI
URL: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK573682/
Content: The inhibition of glutamine metabolism has been linked to ROS overproduction, which can devastate cancer cells [38, 39]. Mitochondrial glutamine metabolism is a significant anaplerotic step in tumorigenesis. It is often enhanced in cancer cells with increased levels of TCA cycle metabolites . Therefore, inhibiting GLS could effectively starve cancer cells of the glutamine essential to their survival and prevent further glutathione synthesis, thus increasing cancer cell exposure to excessive ROS [...] and via glutaminase II pathway. 
   Glutamine metabolism in the tumor microenvironment can impact the development of cancers. 

1. Introduction [...] Due to its crucial role in energy regulation and biosynthesis, targeting glutamine metabolism has the potential to affect a broad spectrum of cancers. In addition to GLS inhibition, the role of oncogenes and tumor suppressors in regulating glutamine metabolism makes it a promising venture for therapeutic strategies. However, while many drugs have been synthesized to target glutamine metabolism from its initial transport into the cell to its conversion to α-KG, most are still in preclinical [...] inhibited cell growth and induced cell death in pancreatic cancer cells. The effect of asparaginase can largely be reversed through the reintroduction of small amounts of glutamine . [...] as pseudohypoxia . Pseudohypoxia, in turn, facilitates tumor cell growth.
