nvironment (Vaupel _et al_, 1989). In tumors, glutamine levels can be profoundly reduced when compared to the surrounding normal tissues and plasma (Roberts _et al_, 1956; Rivera _et al_, 1988; Marquez _et al_, 1989). In addition, a spatial examination of amino acid levels in cancer cell xenografts has found glutamine to
