Title: SLC7A11/xCT-mediated Cystine Uptake Regulates Intracellular ...
URL: https://ar.iiarjournals.org/content/45/1/65
Content: This study provides new insights into the role of xCT in the lymphatic endothelium. Our results revealed that xCT functions as a cystine transporter in LECs and contributes to the regulation of intracellular GSH levels _via_ cystine uptake. In addition, xCT protects against oxidative stress and promotes cell proliferation under oxidative stress. Our results are similar to those observed in vascular endothelial cells: xCT inhibition with erastin, a specific xCT inhibitor, reduces cystine uptake [...] Copyright © 2025 International Institute of Anticancer Research (Dr. George J. Delinasios), All rights reserved.

